[Thm comb of arXiv:2609.02346, 'Regularised double shuffle relations for planar \AZVs{}'] Let $\Omega$ be a set (resp. $(\Omega,+)$ be a semigroup).
	 The products $\shuffle^T$  (resp. $\cshuffle^T$ ) of $\mathcal{PT}_\Omega$ are defined explicitly for any pair $(t,s)\in\mathcal{PT}_\Omega^2$ by:
	 \begin{align*}

	 	t \shuffle^T s = \sum_{\sigma\in\Sh(k+1,l+1)} \sigma(t,s) \quad
	 	\left(\text{\normalfont{ resp. }} 
	 	 t \cshuffle^T s = \sum_{\sigma\in\QSh(k+1,l+1)} \sigma(t,s) \right)
	 \end{align*}
	 where $k+1$ (resp. $l+1$) is the number of nodes in the rightmost (resp. leftmost) branch of $t$ (resp. of $s$).

