[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2608.17449, 'Spectral Simplicity and Joint Eigenvalue Densities\\ for a Non-Gaussian Brownian Time Chan'] There is a deterministic $C<\infty$ such that, for every $n\ge1$ and
$x,y\in D$,
\begin{equation}
 K_n(x,y)\le C+\log^+\frac1{|x-y|}.

\end{equation}
Moreover, for every compact $K\Subset D$ there is $C_K<\infty$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \left|K_n(x,y)-\log^+\frac1{|x-y|\vee2^{-n}}\right|\le C_K,
 \qquad x,y\in K,\quad n\ge1.

\end{equation}

