[Lemma 37 (Generalized Birkhoff's ergodic theorem) of arXiv:2511.13404, 'Asymptotic stability and mean ergodicity of Feller processes on Polish spaces'] Let $\Phi$ be a Markov process on a probability space $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\P)$ with unique invariant measure $\mu$. Let $\P^\mu$ be the distribution of $\Phi$ with initial distribution $\mu$. Suppose $f\ge0$ satisfying $\langle f,\mu\rangle=\infty$ then $\P^\mu$-a.s. $\omega\in\Omega$. 
    \begin{equation*}
        \lim\limits_{t\to\infty}\frac{1}{t}\int_0^t f(\Phi_s(\omega))\d s =\infty.
    \end{equation*}

