[Lemma lem:row-norm of arXiv:2608.07410, 'Extreme least singular values of random row submatrices\\ with bounded-density subgaussian'] For every $A>0$ there is $R=R(A,\xi)$ such that, for
$X=(\xi_1,\dots,\xi_m)$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb P\{\|X\|_2>R\sqrt m\}\le e^{-Am}
\end{equation}
for all sufficiently large $m$.

