[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2512.02855, 'Loewner--Kufarev entropy and large deviations of the Hastings--Levitov model'] The measures $\tilde \mu_{n,m} =\sum\limits_{i=1}^mL_{i}^{n,m}(d\theta)\mathds{1}_{\left[\frac{i-1}{m}, \frac{i}{m}\right)}(t)dt$, indexed by $n$, satisfy a large deviation principle in $\mathcal{M}_{1}(S^1 \times [0,1])$ with the rate $n$ and the rate function 
\begin{align*}
    I_m(\mu) = 
    \begin{cases}
        \frac{1}{m}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{m}H(\nu_i|\lambda), \text{ if }\mu(d\theta,dt) = \sum\limits_{i=1}^{m}\nu_i(d\theta)\mathds{1}_{[\frac{i-1}{m},\frac{i}{m})}(t)dt \text{ with } \nu_i\in\mathcal{M}_{1}(S^{1}),\\
        +\infty, \text{ otherwise}.
    \end{cases}
\end{align*}

