Let $(U_k)_{k\in\Z}$ be a sequence of independent copies of $U$ and let for $m\in\Z$
\bas{\bX^\theta(m)=(X(\theta,U_{k+m}))_{k\in-\N_0}.
}
Note that for all $m\in\N$, $f(\theta)=\E[g(\bX^{\theta}(m))]$ and using that  $g$ is Lipschitz continuous with constant $1$ as mapping on $\ell^d_\varrho$ by \cite{DereichAdamconvergence2024} we get that
