[Lemma lem:square-constrained-bonds of arXiv:2608.23545, 'Eulerian walkers on $\Z^2$ have range exponent $2/3$'] There are constants $c,C>0$ such that the following holds for every $x\in\mathbb Z^2$
		and every integer $r\geq1$.  For bond percolation on $\mathbb Z^2$ with parameter
		$1/2$,
		\begin{equation}
			\mathbb P_{1/2}\left\{
			\begin{array}{c}
				\text{there is an open path from $x$ to $\{y:|y-x|_\infty=r\}$ inside}\\
				\text{$\{y:|y-x|_\infty\leq r\}$ containing no translate of $P_\star$,}\\
				\text{in either direction, as a consecutive subpath}
			\end{array}
			\right\}
			\leq Ce^{-cr}\, .
		\end{equation}

