{"artifact_digest":"sha256:d2c15d5cba95ca9d60d8bcd4f1f3f8862c1a1f1c29cbcbf934687858934855a6","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/d2/d2c15d5cba95ca9d60d8bcd4f1f3f8862c1a1f1c29cbcbf934687858934855a6.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:043de0320d225d81cf01f1c00882b747ce76b6b92148de1b44e1edd49b621b00","bundle_entry_key":"2607-22362-lemma-7-piecewise-constant-approximati","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_078","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_078.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2607-22362-lemma-7-piecewise-constant-approximati","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Let $Q_n$ be as in Lemma~\ref{SA: partition} and set $\alpha_n [ v ] := Q_n (\alpha [ v ])$ for $n\in \mathbb N$.\ 
Using the notation from Lemma~\ref{SA: partition}, we observe that 
\begin{align*}
\pi_t \alpha_n [ v ] = \sum_{j = 1}^{N_n} \langle \alpha [ v ], e^n_j \rangle_{\M} \, \pi_t u^n_j &= \sum_{j = 1}^{N_n} \langle \pi_{t^n_j} \alpha [ v ], e^n_j \rangle_{\M}\, \pi_t u^n_j \1_{\{t^n_j < t\}},
\end{align*}
