[Lemma PZI of arXiv:2604.11761, 'The smallest singular value of signed random combinatorial matrices'] Let $X$ be a nonnegative random variable with $\textbf{E}[X^4] < \infty$. Then, for $0 \leq \lambda < \sqrt{\textbf{E}[X^2]}$ we have
\begin{align*}
\textbf{P}\left(X > \lambda\right) \geq \frac{(\textbf{E}[X^2] - \lambda^2)^2}{\textbf{E}[X^4]}.
\end{align*}

