body:
[Proposition prop:exists_varphi of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] For almost-every $\omega$, whenever $b \in \mathcal{B}_\omega$, the set $\pmb{\xi}^b$ is countable. Furthermore, there exists a function $\varphi:\mathfrak{X} \to [-\infty,\infty)$ with $\operatorname{supp}(\varphi) = \pmb{\xi}^{b}$  such that $b = W\star \varphi$. For this choice of $\varphi$, we have that
    \begin{equation} 
    b(x,t) = \varphi(\xi) + W^\xi(0,0;x,t),\quad \forall \xi \in \pmb{\xi}^{b},\text{ and } (x,t) \in \mathfrak{C}^b(\xi).
    \end{equation}

