[Prop quantitative-interpolation of arXiv:2609.03751, 'Sparse bounds for maximal rough singular integrals'] Let \(1<p\leq2\), so that \(p'\geq2\), and choose
\begin{equation}
    r:=\lceil2p'\rceil+1.
\end{equation}
Then \(r\) is an integer satisfying
\[
    2p'<r\leq2p'+2.
\]
Set
\[
    \delta_\ast
    :=
    \min\left\{
      \frac{\kappa}{2},
      \frac{1-\kappa}{2},
      \delta_0
    \right\}>0,
\]
where \(\delta_0\) is the exponent in
Proposition~(prop:microlocal-endpoints of the paper).  For every \(s\geq2\),
\(n\geq1\), and \(1\leq\iota\leq2^d\), one has
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
 &\left\|
   \sum_{j\in\mathbb Z}
   \sum_{Q\in\mathfrak V_{j-s}^{n,\iota}}
      \varepsilon_{J(Q)}
      T_jb_Q\,\mathbf1_{J(Q)^\iota}
 \right\|_{L^{p'}(\mathbb R^d)}
 \\
 &\qquad\lesssim_d
 p'\,2^{-2n/p'}2^{-\delta_\ast s/p'}
 \|\Omega\|_{L^\infty(S^{d-1})}
 \|b\|_{\dot{\mathcal X}_1(\mathcal Q)}
 |Q_0|^{1/p'}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
This proves (equation equ3.24 of the paper) with
\(\delta=\delta_\ast\).

