[Definition 12 of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] [Loop decomposition of a region] 
Given $M \subset M_0$ and $R \in REG(M)$. $R$ is called \textit{loop decomposable} if it can be divided into loops, i.e., $\exists \psi_1,\ \psi_2,\ \cdots ,\ \psi_k \in LOOP(M)$ ($k \in \mathbf{N}$) such that
\begin{equation*}
R=|\psi_1|_0 \cup |\psi_2|_0 \cup \cdots \cup |\psi_k|_0.
\end{equation*}

[Theorem thm:gaussian of arXiv:2608.28169, 'characteristic polynomial of self-normalized random matrices'] Assume $X_{11} \in {\mathrm{DAN}}$. For integers $k_1,\ldots, k_\ell\geqslant 1$, we then have the convergence of traces
    \begin{equation}
        \left(\operatorname{Tr} \left[ {\mathbf Y}^{k_1}_n \right], \dots, \operatorname{Tr} \left[ {\mathbf Y}^{k_\ell}_n \right] \right) \stackrel{\rm d}{\rightarrow} \left(\1_{\{2\mid k_1\}}+\sqrt{k_1}Z_{k_1}',\dots,\1_{\{2\mid k_\ell\}}+\sqrt{k_\ell}Z_{k_\ell}'\right) \,,\qquad n\to\infty\,,
    \end{equation}
    and the limiting characteristic polynomial is  
    \begin{equation}

        p_n(z) \stackrel{\rm d}{\rightarrow}  
        \sqrt{1 - z^{2}} \cdot \exp \left( - \sum_{k \geqslant 1} 
        \frac{z^k}{\sqrt{k}} Z_k' \right) \,, \qquad n\to\infty,\, z\in \mathbb{D}\,,
    \end{equation}
    where $(Z_k')_{k \geqslant 1}$ are i.i.d.\ standard Gaussian random variables. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

