[Proposition prop|IdempotentFixedPoints of arXiv:2504.08935, 'Higher-Order Derivatives of First-Passage Percolation with Respect to the Environment'] If $\psi:R\to R$ is an idempotent function, then the set of its fixed points is equal to its range, i.e. \begin{align}
