[Theorem 17 of arXiv:2604.09365, 'Cotlar martingale transforms and related singular integrals'] Suppose $d>2$ is odd so that $d+1=2n$ for and integer  $n>1$. Let $R_1$ be the first Riesz transform on $\R^d$.  Consider the Cotlar matrix $\BH_{2n}$ given in \eqref{HilbertMatrix}.  Then the projection of the Cotlar martingale transform $\BH_{2n}*M_t^f$ is $R_1f$. That is,   
\begin{align}
T_{\BH_{2n}}f=R_1f
\end{align}
and 
\begin{align}
\|R_1f\|_p\leq \cot\left(\frac{\pi}{2 p^*}\right)\|f\|_p, \,\, p = 2^k\,\,  \text{or}\,\,  p=\frac{2^k}{2^k-1}, k\in \bN.
\end{align}

[Lemma prop: QV proc in the critical regime of arXiv:2505.05921, 'Limit Theorems for step reinforced random walks\\ with regularly varying memory'] {}
    Let $\{S_n\}_{n\geq 0}$ be the SRRW-RVM with zero mean, unit variance innovation sequence $\{\xi_n\}$. Assume $p=p_c$ and $\{v_n\}$ is unbounded. Then the quadratic variation process of $\{\mathpalette\wide@cap{M}_{n,\lfloor nt\rfloor}\}$ satisfies
    $\ang{\,\mathpalette\wide@cap{M}\,}_{n,\lfloor nt\rfloor} \to 1$ in $L^1$, for all $t>0$.

