{"artifact_digest":"sha256:784f2db83ffa1519bcf7e2273e1cef3e9f43cea56097eae64235cd061d5acfc2","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/78/784f2db83ffa1519bcf7e2273e1cef3e9f43cea56097eae64235cd061d5acfc2.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:4392b5fb64c0455cb1306d5dcd7991dd009f9c5bf9ffecd1275a1650d0a6a7e5","bundle_entry_key":"2604-26819-lemma-11-lemma-11","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_022","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_022.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2604-26819-lemma-11-lemma-11","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Let $ v = \matrix{\cos(-\theta) & \sin(-\theta)}^\top \in \bbS^1 $ for some $ \theta \in [0,2\pi) $. 
To compute the moment generating function of $ \inprod{X}{v} $, it suffices to consider $ \lambda > 0 $ since otherwise we can use $ -v $ in place of $v$. 
Denote $ s \coloneqq r \lambda $. 
Then 
\begin{align}
    \expt{\exp\paren{ \lambda \inprod{X}{v} }}
    &= \frac{1}{3} \sum_{j = 0}^2 \exp\paren{ \lambda \inprod{r \matrix{\cos(\theta_j) \\ \sin(\theta_j)}}{\matrix{\cos(-\theta) \\ \sin(-\theta)}} }
    = \frac{1}{3} \sum_{j = 0}^2 \exp\paren{ s \cos(\theta_j + \theta) } \notag \\
    &\le \frac{e^s + 2 e^{-s/2}}{3}
    \le \exp\paren{ \frac{3s^2}{16\log(2)} } , \notag ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:ab514408b0299f55c5c5ee8ad21f8451005d3eaa9d611451ce65b24a24365bcb","revision_digest":"sha256:c63d06038d0aebc75393e9a4e49ccde36cf93f68fc97befdd4aecaa6979300a5","source_id":"arxiv:2604.26819","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

