[Proposition prop:coercivity_optimal of arXiv:2609.03164, 'Energy Decay Induced by Localized Coercivity in the 3D Navier--Stokes Equations'] Let $\chi_\omega\in L^\infty(\mathbb{T}^3)$ be nonnegative and let
$K_{\min}\ge 0$.
Define
\begin{equation}

\alpha_\omega(K_{\min})
:=
\inf_{v\in V\setminus\{0\}}
\frac{
\nu \|\nabla v\|_{L^2(\mathbb{T}^3)}^2
+
K_{\min}\|\chi_\omega^{1/2} v\|_{L^2(\mathbb{T}^3)}^2
}{
\|v\|_{L^2(\mathbb{T}^3)}^2
}.
\end{equation}
Then, for all $v\in V$,
\begin{equation}

\nu \|\nabla v\|_{L^2(\mathbb{T}^3)}^2
+
K_{\min}\|\chi_\omega^{1/2} v\|_{L^2(\mathbb{T}^3)}^2
\ge
\alpha_\omega(K_{\min}) \|v\|_{L^2(\mathbb{T}^3)}^2.
\end{equation}
Moreover, $\alpha_\omega(K_{\min})>0$ if and only if a coercivity inequality of
the form (equation eq:coercivity of the paper) holds, and in that case
$\alpha_\omega(K_{\min})$ is the largest admissible constant.

[Definition IP-convergence1 of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] A sequence $\{x_{n}\}_{n\in \mathrm{FS}(D)}$ is said
to be \textit{IP-convergent} to $x^{\ast }\in X$ if for every open
neighborhood $U\ni x^{\ast }$ there exists $L$ such that 
\begin{equation}
x_{n}\in U\qquad \text{for all }n\in \mathrm{FS}(q_{L},q_{L+1},q_{L+2},\dots
).  
\end{equation}

[Lemma 64 of arXiv:2609.02850, 'Canonical-row Chern flow on Bott--Samelson towers:\\ realizable-volume models for Schubert'] For all admissible homogeneous components,
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal R_{M,r+1}\,\mathscr D_i^{(z)}\,\mathcal R_{M,r}
 =-\mathscr K_i^{(z)}.
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
 \omega(-\mathscr K_i^{(z)})\omega=\Gamma_{n-i}^{(z)}.
\end{equation}

[Theorem 10 (Critical logarithmic estimate) of arXiv:2608.17540, 'Pathwise stability for one-dimensional SDEs driven by Brownian motion and a symmetric stab'] Assume Assumptions~\ref{ass:baseline}--\ref{ass:solutions} and $B,A,S<1$. Suppose $\wt\eta=1/\alpha$ and set
\[
  \Theta:=\max\{B,A,S\}.
\]
Then there exists $C>0$ such that, for $0<\Theta<1$,
\begin{equation}
\sup_{0\le t\le T}\E|X_t-\wt X_t|^{\alpha-1}
\le C\left[|x_0-\wt x_0|^{\alpha-1}+\left(\log\frac1\Theta\right)^{-1}\right].
\end{equation}
When $\Theta=0$, the right-hand side is understood as $C|x_0-\wt x_0|^{\alpha-1}$ by the limiting convention.

