[Def relative-steel-condition of arXiv:2608.26876, 'Local Bousfield classes via homological support'] We say that the \emph{$A$-relative steel condition} holds for $\cat T$ if the comparison map $\pi\colon\Spc^h(\cat T^c)\to\Spc(\cat T^c)$ restricts to a bijection 
	\begin{equation}
		\Supph(A)\xra{\sim} \Supp(A).
	\end{equation}
	The $A=\unit$ case reduces to the usual steel condition ((def:steel-condition of the paper)).

[Definition 10 of arXiv:2604.09365, 'Cotlar martingale transforms and related singular integrals'] For any $t>0$ and  $1<p<\infty$, define
\begin{align}
\beta_p := \sup \Big\{\frac{\|Y_t\|_p}{\|X_t\|_p}\Big\}, 
\end{align}
where the $\sup$ is taken over all pairs $(X, Y)$ of martingales such that $Z=X+iY$ is a conformal martingale.

