[Prop BoundsCorGFF of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] Let $G^{D}$ indicate the Green function of $D$. Then, there exist finite constants $k < K$, that uniformly on $x,y\in D$ and $0<\varepsilon, \delta<1$
    \begin{equation*}
    \ln\left (\frac{1}{\varepsilon \lor \delta \lor |x-y|}\right )+k \leq
        G^{D}_{\varepsilon,\delta}(x,y) \leq \ln\left (\frac{1}{\varepsilon \lor \delta \lor |x-y|}\right )+K.     
    \end{equation*}

[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2606.11845, 'Stochastic epidemic model with varying infectivity and waning immunity: the law of large n'] As $N\to\infty$, for any $T>0$,
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{1}{N}\E\left[\sum_{k=1}^N\sup_{0\le t\le T}|B^N_k(t)-B_k(t)|\right]\to0\,.
    \end{align*}

