[Lemma tail_bound_truncated_selection_set of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Fix $c \in (0,m+1)$ and assume the choice sequence $\mathbf x$ satisfies Assumption~$\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}$(item:geq1 of the paper),~(item:hI of the paper) with $\varepsilon<1-c/(m+1)$, and $A_i\geq m+1$ for all $i\in\{I_{\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}},\ldots,n\}$. Then, there exists  $\beta>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}(|\mathcal{S}_n(a_1)\cap\{I_{\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}},\ldots,n\}|< ch_n^+) = o(n^{-\beta}).
\end{equation}
Additionally, suppose that $\mathbf x$ satisfies Assumption~$\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}$(item:Jn of the paper) for some $\eta\in(0,1-c/(m+1))$. Then, there exists $\xi\in(0,1)$ such that
\begin{equation} 
\P{|\mathcal{S}_n(f_1)\cap \{I_{\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}},\ldots, n\}|<c\log F_n}=\mathcal{O}(F_n^{-\xi}).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 14 (Generalized resolvent identity) of arXiv:2609.03924, 'Beyond normal fluctuations in local laws for Wigner matrices'] For $H=H^*\in\C^{N\times N}$ and $z_j\in\C\setminus\R$ denote $G_j:=(H-z_j)^{-1}$, $j=1,2$. For any $k,l\in\N$ it holds that
\begin{equation}
G_1^kG_2^l = \sum_{u=1}^k (-1)^{k-u} \binom{l+k-u-1}{l-1} \frac{G_1^u}{(z_1-z_2)^{l+k-u}} + \sum_{v=1}^l (-1)^{l-v} \binom{l+k-v-1}{k-1} \frac{G_2^v}{(z_2-z_1)^{l+k-v}}.

\end{equation}

