body:
[Proposition 12 of arXiv:2512.10199, 'Explicit correlation functions for the six-vertex model in the free-fermion regime'] Let $x^1,\dots,x^k \in \midedge_n$ and let $y^1,\ldots,y^k$ be suitable neighbouring mid-edges, so that $y^i - x^i \in \{(0,0), e^1, e^2, e^3\}$ for each $i$.  Then
        \begin{equation} 
              P_n\left[\bigcap_{i=1}^k \{\orho(x^i) = y^i\} \right] =  \prod_{i = 1}^{k} K_{(0,0)}(x^i,y^i) \sum_{\theta \in \{0,1\}^2 } \frac{C_\theta \det(K_\theta)}{Z^{\gen}_n} q_\theta \det_{i,j = 1}^{k} K_\theta^{-1} (y^i,x^j),
        \end{equation}
        where $q_\theta = \exp\left(\frac{\pi \iota}{n}\big(\theta,\sum_{i=1}^k (y^i - x^i)\big) \right)$, with $\big(\theta,\sum_{i=1}^k (y^i - x^i)\big)$ being the standard inner product on $\mathbb{R}^2$.

