[Thm thm-P2 of arXiv:2609.02552, 'Resolvent Estimates for the Stokes Operator \\ in a Three-Dimensional Lipschitz Domain'] Let $d=3$ and $\lambda\in \Sigma_\theta$.
Let $(u, \phi )$ be the same as in Theorem (thm-P1 of the paper).
Suppose $x_0 \in \partial\Omega$ and $0< r<  r_0$.
Then, for $2\le q< 3+\varepsilon$ and $p=\frac{2q}{3}$, 
\begin{equation}
\left(
\fint_{B(x_0, r)\cap \Omega} |\phi -\beta|^q \right)^{1/q}
+\left(\fint_{B(x_0, r)\cap \partial\Omega}
|\phi -\beta|^p \right)^{1/p} 
\le C M_p(|\nabla u|) (r),
\end{equation}
where 
 $\beta=\fint_{B(x_0, r) \cap \partial\Omega} \phi $ and  $C$ depends only on $q$ and $\Omega$.

[Thm main_result of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] Let $P_t$ be the Markov semigroup of (equation e:SNS of the paper). Let $V_{\alpha}: \mathcal{C}^{-\kappa} \rightarrow \mathbf{R}$ defined above be the Lyapunov function for the Markov process. There exist some positive constants $0 < \alpha_0\leq 1$ and $C > 0$ such that, if the noise $\xi$ satisfies Assumption~(as:noise of the paper) and $\limsup_{k\rightarrow \infty} |\phi_k| \leq \frac{1}{2}\alpha_0$\,, then there exists some $\gamma > 0$ such that for any $t \geq 1$ and $x\in \mathcal{C}^{-\kappa}$, we have
\begin{equ}

    \big(P_{t} V_{2\alpha_0}\big)(x) \leq C e^{-\gamma t} V_{2 \alpha_0}(x) + C\;.
\end{equ}
As a result, the solution to (equation e:SNS of the paper) admits at least one invariant measure $\mu_\star$. 
Moreover, for any $N \in \mathbf{N}^*$ there exists some $\gamma_N > 0$ such that for any $x \in L^2 \cap \mathcal{C}^{-\kappa}$ and $t \geq 0$ we have 
\begin{equ}

    \big(P_{t} V^N_{2\alpha_0}\big)(x) \leq C^N e^{-\gamma_N t} \|x\|^N + (CN)^{2N}\;.
\end{equ} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor_gammfourmoment of arXiv:2509.18045, 'Density convergence on Markov diffusion chaos via Stein's method'] Assume the above setup. Under the conditions that  the first four moments of $F_n$ converge to the first four moments of $\mathcal{Z}$ and 
\begin{align}

    \sup_{n\in\mathbb{N}}\brac{\E{\frac{1}{F_n^6}\mathds{1}_{\{F_n\leq 0 \}}}+\E{\frac{1}{\Gamma(F_n)^4}}+\E{\frac{1}{F_n^4}}+\E{\autobracket*{L(\Gamma(F_n)-F_n}^2}}<\infty, 
\end{align}
then the densities $p_{F_n}(x)$ converges to the density $p_\mathcal{Z}(x)$ for every $x\in \mathbb{R}$.

