[Proposition proposition424 of arXiv:2606.01664, 'Brown measure convergence for the spectrum of polynomials in Ginibre matrices'] For any $A>2m$, suppose that $\mathbb{E}_\xi|D_U(\xi)|^2\leq N^{-A}$, then we can find $\alpha_*=\alpha_*(\mathfrak{p})$ depending only on the polynomial $\mathfrak{p}$, and $C>0$ depending only on $\mathfrak{p}$, as well as a subspace $\mathcal{P}\subset M_m(\mathbb{C})$
consisting entirely of non-invertible matrices, such that
\begin{equation}
\operatorname{dist}(U_j K_z,\mathcal{P})^2+\sum_{i,\ell}\operatorname{dist}(U_iH_\ell,\mathcal{P})^2\leq C N^{-A/2\alpha_*}.  
\end{equation}

