[Defn 21 (doubling) of arXiv:2604.15191, 'Quantitative Stability of Many-Marginal Schr\"odinger Bridge'] A probability distribution $\rho\in\ms P(\mb T^d)$ is \emph{doubling} with coefficient $c > 0$ if
\begin{align*}
\rho\big(B_{\mb T^d}(x, 2r)\big) \leq c \rho\big(B_{\mb T^d}(x, r)\big)
\end{align*}
holds for any $x\in\mb T^d$ and $r > 0$. 
\myqed

