[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2607.20714, 'High Minima of Gaussian Processes: Overshoots and Minimizer Locations'] The following conditions are equivalent:
\begin{align*}
 \textnormal{(i)}\quad &\mathcal E_R(\mu)>0\quad\text{for every }\mu\in\cM(K);
 &\textnormal{(ii)}\quad &\sigma_*^2>0;\\
 \textnormal{(iii)}\quad
 &\Pp\{M>u_0\}>0\quad\text{for some }u_0\geq0;
 &\textnormal{(iv)}\quad
 &\Pp\{M>u\}>0\quad\text{for every }u\in\mathbb R.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition of arXiv:2512.12124, 'A discontinuous percolation phase transition on the hierarchical lattice'] We say that a set $U \subset \Lambda_{M_g+jr,\infty}$ is non-bad if all its elements are either good or mediocre. For a good or mediocre block $\varphi \in \Lambda_{M_g+jr,\infty}$, we define
    \begin{equation*}
        S(\varphi) = \begin{cases}
            |K_{\max}(\varphi)| & \text{ if } \varphi \text{ is good}\\
            \sum_{\varphi^\prime \in \chi_r(\varphi)} |K_{\max}(\varphi^\prime)| & \text{ if } \varphi \text{ is mediocre}
        \end{cases}.
    \end{equation*}

[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2607.08696, 'Spectrum of Directed Inhomogeneous Random Graphs'] Fix $R>0$. There exist constants $c$ and $C$ depending only on $R$ and on the constants in Assumption \ref{ass:rank-one} such that the following holds: if $\psi_n$ is integer-valued, such that $\psi_n \gg 1$, $\psi_n <
n$ and $\scaling \psi_n/n \ge C \log(n)$, then for any $z \in \mathcal{B}(0,R)$ it holds
\begin{equation} 
    \p\left( 
    \bigcup^{n-1}_{i=3\psi_n}
\left\{\sigma_{n-i}\left(\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{\scaling}}{{A}_n}-zI_n\right)\le c\frac{i}{n}\right\}\right)\le\frac{4}{n^2}.
\end{equation}

