Otherwise, if $c'-c< 0$
\begin{align*}
e^{-ct}\int_0^t e^{-(c'-c)r}\text{d} r= e^{-c't}\int_0^t e^{-(c-c')(t-r)}\text{d} r\le \frac{e^{-c't}}{c-c'}.
\end{align*}
