body:
[Proposition 15 (Explicit expression of Hermite polynomials) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] For any $n\in\N_0$, one has 
\begin{equation}

 H_n(x) = n!\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor n/2 \rfloor}
 \frac{(-1)^k}{2^kk!(n-2k)!}x^{n-2k}\;.
\end{equation} 
The inverse relation is given by 
\begin{equation}

 x^n = n!\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor n/2 \rfloor}
 \frac{1}{2^kk!(n-2k)!}H_{n-2k}(x)\;.
\end{equation}

