[Lemma 119 (High moments of one-dimensional Gaussian chaoses) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $g_{\mathbb R}$ be a standard real Gaussian and let $g_{\mathbb C}$ be a
standard circular complex Gaussian.  For independent copies
$g_1,\ldots,g_m$ of the indicated type,
\begin{align}

  \lim_{p\to\infty}
  \frac{\|\prod_{\nu=1}^m g_{\mathbb R,\nu}\|_{L^p}}
       {p^{m/2}}
  &=e^{-m/2},\\

  \lim_{p\to\infty}
  \frac{\|\prod_{\nu=1}^m g_{\mathbb C,\nu}\|_{L^p}}
       {p^{m/2}}
  &=(2e)^{-m/2}.
\end{align}
If $H_m$ is the probabilists' Hermite polynomial, then
\begin{equation}

  \lim_{p\to\infty}
  \frac{\|H_m(g_{\mathbb R})\|_{L^p}}
       {p^{m/2}}
  =\left(\frac me\right)^{m/2}.
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}

  \lim_{p\to\infty}
  \frac{\|H_m(g_{\mathbb R})\|_{L^p}}
       {\|\prod_{\nu=1}^m g_{\mathbb R,\nu}\|_{L^p}}
  =m^{m/2}.
\end{equation}

[Theorem thm:stationary_bounds of arXiv:2607.13748, 'Load Balancing with Individually Heterogeneous Servers'] Suppose that each server in the system has a finite buffer of length $b$ and Assumption~(asm:arrival_service_rates of the paper) holds. Also assume that for $\varepsilon>0$ there exists $\varrho>0$ such that $\mathbb{P}(\varsigma^n+\nu^n>\varepsilon)>\varrho$ for all $n\in \mathbb{N}$. Then there exist constants $C_{1,\varepsilon},C_{2,\varepsilon},C_{3,\varepsilon}$, uniform in $n$ and over all tie-breaking policies where a stationary version exists, such that
\begin{align}

\mathbb{E}\left[|X_1^{\pi,n}(\infty)|\mid \varsigma^n+\nu^n>\varepsilon\right]&<C_{1,\varepsilon},\\

\mathbb{E}\left[|X_2^{\pi,n}(\infty)|\mid \varsigma^n+\nu^n>\varepsilon\right]&<C_{2,\varepsilon},\\

\mathbb{E}\left[|X_3^{\pi,n}(\infty)|\mid \varsigma^n+\nu^n>\varepsilon\right]&<C_{3,\varepsilon}n^{-1/2},
\end{align}
for all $n\in\mathbb{N}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

