[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2607.14718, 'Anchored Nash inequalities and heat kernel bounds for a class of random conductance models'] Suppose that \eqref{a2-2-1} holds and there exist $m_{0} > d$ and $p, q \in (1, \infty]$ satisfying

  \begin{align}
    \frac{1}{p} + \frac{1}{q} \;\leq\; \frac{m_{0}-2}{d},
  \end{align}

  such that

  \begin{align}
    \sup_{R \geq 1} \Norm{\theta^{-1}}{p, B(R)}
    + \sup_{R \geq 1}\Norm{\mu_{m_{0}}}{q, B(R)}
    \;<\;
    \infty.
  \end{align}

  Then, there exists $C_{15} \in (0, \infty)$ such that

  \begin{align*}
    \sum_{\substack{z \in \boldsymbol{V} \\ d(y,z) > 2\eta(y)}}
    \mspace{-18mu}W(y, z)\, d(y, z)^{m_{0}}
    \;\leq\;
    C_{15}\, R_{0}^{1/p+1/q} \widetilde{\cM}^2\, \eta^{m_{0}-2}(y)\, \theta(y),
    \qquad \forall\, y \in \boldsymbol{V},
  \end{align*}

  with $\widetilde{\cM} \ldef \sup_{R \geq 1} \bigl(\Norm{\theta^{-1}}{p, B(R)} + \Norm{\mu_{m_{0}}}{q, B(R)}\bigr)$ and $R_{0} \geq 1$ being the constant in Assumption \ref{a2-2}.

