[Proposition p:skewBM RK i of arXiv:2411.04773, 'Meeting of squared Bessel flow lines and application to the skew Brownian motion'] For any $r\ge 0$, a.s.
\begin{equation}
    L_{\tau^0_z}^r = \inf \{ x\ge \max(r,z): \mathcal S_{r,x}(0)= Y_x\}.
\end{equation}

\noindent As a result, Theorem (thm: skewBM RK of the paper) (i) holds (take $(\mathcal S, Y, z)$ in place of $(\mathcal S,Y^0,z)$ in Section (s:meetingL of the paper)).

[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2606.06859, 'The rectangular finite free heat flow'] The equations (\ref{eq:ode}) are equivalent to the vector equality
    \begin{equation} 
    \dot{r} = \nabla H(r),
    \end{equation}
    where $\nabla$ indicates the gradient with respect to $(r_1, \dots, r_d)$, and
    \begin{equation} 
    H(r) = \log \left[ \left( \prod_{i=1}^d r_i^{n+1} \right) \prod_{1 \le i<j \le d} (r_i - r_j)(r_i + r_j) \right]. 
    \end{equation}

