[Proposition 63 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] The cusps of the surface~$S_{\operatorname{Romb}}$ are light-like. In particular, as~${r_{i,q'}\ni z\to \mathcal Z_i}$, 
\begin{equation*}
\vartheta\circ\mathcal Z^{-1}(z)-\vartheta_i=\frac{\overline{G} (q')}{G(q')}(z-\mathcal Z_i)+\Ordo\left((z-\mathcal Z_i)^2\right),
\end{equation*}
where
\begin{equation*}
\left|\frac{\overline{G}(q')}{G(q')}\right|=1.
\end{equation*}

