[Prop unique of arXiv:2509.26254, '$K$-Branching Random Walk with Noisy Selection: \\ \Large Large Population Limits and Phas'] There is a  unique traveling wave solution $(G,\nu)$, which is given by
 \begin{equation}
 G = f_{\bm y}, \ \ \text{ where }
\bm{y} := \left( 0,\left(-(\chi\vee 0) - (j-1)\nu)\right)_{j=1}^K\right),
