[Definition 2 (Strong levelwise variation contact) of arXiv:2608.06393, 'Intrinsic Tangential Hadamard Differentiability of Rough-BSDE Solution Maps'] Fix $\mathbf x\in WG\Omega_p(E)$. Let $\varepsilon_n\to0$ with
$\varepsilon_n\neq0$, let
$\tau_n=(h_n,\kappa_n)\to\tau=(h,\kappa)$ in
$\mathbb T_{\mathbf x}^p$, and let
$\mathbf x_n=(1,x_n,\mathbb x_n)\in WG\Omega_p(E)$. We say that
$\mathbf x_n$ has strong levelwise variation contact with
$(\varepsilon_n,\tau_n)$ at $\mathbf x$ if
\begin{equation}
 \|x_n-x-\varepsilon_n h_n\|_{p\text{-var}}
 +\|\mathbb x_n-\mathbb x-\varepsilon_n\kappa_n\|_{q\text{-var};2}
 =o(|\varepsilon_n|).
\end{equation}
Such a sequence is called an admissible secant at $\mathbf x$.

