[Corollary cor:fischer of arXiv:2609.01672, '\textbf{All-Minors Matrix-Tree Theory for Superport Networks:\\ Completed Quotient-Inciden'] For all \(I,J\subseteq N\),
\begin{equation}
\boxed{\Psi_I\Psi_J\ge \Psi_{I\cup J}\Psi_{I\cap J}.}
\end{equation}
After normalization by \(\mathcal P_F(1,\ldots,1)\), the coefficients define a strongly Rayleigh probability measure on subsets of \(N\).

[Lemma lem-A2 of arXiv:2512.17727, 'Stochastic transport equation with L\'evy noise'] There exists  a $\mathbb{P}$-full set  $\Omega^{(iv)} \subset \Omega^{(1)}$ and an infinite set $\Upsilon_{1} \subset \Upsilon$  such that for
every $\omega \in \Omega^{(iv)}$ and every $T>0$,
  \begin{equation}
\lim_{ \ensuremath{\varepsilon} \in \Upsilon_{1}\rightarrow 0 }  \sup_{t \in [0,T]} \Big\vert   \int_{\mathbb R^d} u_0(y)\,\theta (\phi^{\ensuremath{\varepsilon}}_t(y))J_t^{\ensuremath{\varepsilon}}(y)\,dy- \int_{\mathbb R^d} u_0(y)\,\theta (\phi_t(y))J_t(y)\,dy \Big\vert=0.
    \end{equation}

