body:
[Theorem thm:Fourier_PF of arXiv:2608.15923, 'Universality of two-dimensional Markovian holonomy fields'] Let $\Sigma_{g,n}$ be a compact connected oriented surface and let ${\mathbb{G}}=(V,E,F)$ be a topological map embedded in $\Sigma_{g,n}$, with every boundary component carried by ${\mathbb{G}}$. Let $(Q_t)$ be a family of central continuous probability densities and assume the graph-level spectral summability condition
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{\lambda\in\widehat G}
 d_\lambda^{2-2g}
 \prod_{f\in F}|a_{|f|}(\lambda)|<\infty.
\end{equation}
Then the partition function has the absolutely convergent expansion
\begin{equation}
 Z_{{\mathbb{G}},G,Q,\mathrm{vol}}(t_1,\ldots,t_n)
 =\sum_{\lambda\in\widehat G}
 \left(\prod_{f\in F}a_{|f|}(\lambda)\right)
 d_\lambda^{2-2g}\prod_{j=1}^n\frac{\chi_\lambda(t_j)}{d_\lambda}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop 15 of arXiv:2604.12334, 'On additive averaging kernels for finite Markov chains'] For $P \in \mathcal{S}(\pi)$ and $G$ a Gibbs kernel defined on some partition $(\mathcal{O}_i)_{i=1}^k$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \KL{\widetilde{\pi}_\alpha}(Q_\alpha\ \|\ \widetilde{\Pi}_\alpha) = (1-\alpha)\KL{\pi} (G\| \Pi) + \alpha \KL{\pi}(P \| \Pi). 
    \end{equation}

[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2606.17859, 'Full $\Gamma-$expansion for the level-two large deviation rate functionals of non-reversib'] For every $0\leq p < \widehat{\mf q}$, the $0-$level set of $\ms J^{(p)}$ is the
convex hull of the $(p+1)-$order metastable states. That is,
\begin{equation*}
\left\{\mu\in \mss P(\bb T): \ms J^{(p)}(\mu) = 0\right\}\,=\, \mss P_{\mc M_{p+1}}.
\end{equation*}

