where $\lambda_1, \dots, \lambda_N$ are the eigenvalues of $G$, and $X_1, \dots, X_k$ are i.i.d. standard complex Gaussian variables. The probability measures associated to these families of variables are denoted by $\mathbb{P}_{\lambda}$ and $\mathbb{P}_{X}$ respectively. 
