In particular, $g^\beta(t) = \P\left(\sigma^{\beta} > t \right) + c$ for some $c \in \R$ and for all $t \in \R_+$. Sending $t \rightarrow \infty$, we see that $c = 0$. We conclude that $\sigma^{\beta} \sim","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:3e8b45c7fd7f0282b2c44baeb76ec825436e648db45d8d71d5d2ccd82cf4a0e4","revision_digest":"sha256:cbc08d6999dcf7935f47a9fa5c92d016f1ef04f9a09c0a5b92b9c9946c77bc09","source_id":"arxiv:2608.27374","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

