[Corollary 8 of arXiv:2607.17943, 'Coadjoint averaging and cross-scale fluxes in a fast-slow stochastic Euler-Arnold system o'] For any bounded smooth function $G: \su(N)\rightarrow \mathbb{R}$, any $t>0$ we have, as $\varepsilon\rightarrow 0$ and then $\delta \rightarrow 0$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{E}_{\Omega_0^{\varepsilon,\delta}=\Omega_0} \int_0^{t\wedge \tau^{\varepsilon,\delta}} G(\Omega_s^{\varepsilon,\delta})ds \rightarrow \mathbf{E}_{Z_0=\pi(\Omega_0)} \int_0^{t\wedge \tau} \overline{G}(Z_s)ds \ .
\end{equation}
where $\overline{G}(z)=\displaystyle{\int_{\mathcal{O}^*(z)}}G(\Omega)dm_z(\Omega)$ is defined in \emph{(\ref{Eq:AveragingLeafwiseCoAdjointsuN})}.

