[Corollary 3 (Combinatorial discrepancy) of arXiv:2605.13107, 'Discrepancy and Fisher information'] Let $v_1,\dots,v_n \in \R^d$ be any fixed vectors, and let $\e_1,\ldots, \e_n$ be independent Rademacher random variables. Then there exists an online algorithm that discards some terms $\e_j v_j$ so that, for each $k$,
	\begin{equation}	
		\norm[\Bigg]{\sum_{j \le k \text{ accepted}} \e_j v_j}_\infty \le 2T
		\quad \text{deterministically},
	\end{equation}
	and
	$$
	\E \#\{\text{discarded}\}
	\le \frac{\pi}{2T} \sum_{j=1}^n \norm{v_j}_2.
	$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem 11 (Simplex additivity for persistence) of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] Let $\phi: K \rightarrow M$ be an admissible triangulation. Let $f: M \rightarrow \RR_{\ge 0}$ be a probability density, $\filt$ be either the Vietoris-Rips or \v Cech complex, and $\rmax_n$ be a radius cutoff parameter. Then there exists a constant $c>0$ so that for all integers $1 \le k \le d$, $\alpha \in (1, \infty)$ and sufficiently large $n$,
    \begin{align} 
        \bigg| \overline{\Pi}_{k, \filt}(nf)(\alpha) - \sum_{\dim\sigma = d} \overline{\Pi}_{k, \filt}(nf|_{\phi(\sigma)})(\alpha) \bigg| \le c \cdot n^{k+1} \rmax_n^{dk+1} (1 + n \rmax_n^d),
    \end{align}
    Furthermore, the persistence functional satisfies the simplex additivity \eqref{eqn:simplex_additivity1} if 
    the radius cutoff satisfies $n \rmax^d_n = o(n^{1/(d^2+d+1)})$.

