[Proposition prop:aux of arXiv:2507.19554, 'Full extremal process in four-dimensional membrane model'] Let $A \subset [0, 1]^4$ be non-empty and open. Let $z_i$ be such that we have $\max_{x\in V_{N}^{K, \delta, i}}h_x^f = h_{z_i}$ 
	and let $\overline{z}$ be such that $\max\{ h_{z_i}: B^{K, i}\subset A\} = h_{\overline{z}}$. Then for all $\epsilon, \delta$
    \begin{equation}
        \lim_{K\rightarrow \infty}\lim\sup_{N\rightarrow \infty} \mbP\lp \max_{x\in V_{N, A}^{K, \delta}}h_x \geq h_{\overline{z}} + \epsilon\rp = 0.
    \end{equation}
    Furthermore, there exists a sequence $(B_K)_{K\geq 1}$ with $B_K \rightarrow \infty$ as $K \rightarrow \infty$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \lim_{K\rightarrow \infty}\lim\sup_{N\rightarrow \infty} \mbP\lp h_{\overline{z}}^f \leq m_{N/K} + B_K\rp = 0.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:stat.dist.alpha=0 of arXiv:2607.10708, 'A class of Markov processes with resetting and applications to cybersecurity'] Let $X=(N,\Lambda,C)$  be a self-exciting PDMP with resetting and $Y=(N,\Lambda)$. Under Assumption (a:finitereset of the paper) holds and with $\alpha=0$, there exists an invariant measure $\Pi$ for $Y$, given by the following, for $\lambda \in ({\lambda^o}, A)$:

\begin{equation} 
    \begin{split}
      \Pi(0, d \lambda) &=\frac{K_0}{{\lambda^o}} \delta_{{\lambda^o}}(d\lambda)\\
      \Pi(1, d \lambda) &=\frac{K_0}{\lambda}\,dG_{\ell}(1, \lambda-{\lambda^o})\\
      \Pi(n, d \lambda) &=\frac{1}{\lambda}  d\overline G_{\ell}(n,\lambda)
    \end{split}

\end{equation}
    with $K_0=\sum_{n=1}^\infty\int_{[{\lambda^o},A)}\lambda \bar{G}_{\ell}(n, (A-\lambda) \textrm{-})\Pi(n-1,d\lambda)$ and
    where $\overline \Pi(n,d\lambda) := \lambda \Pi(n,d\lambda)$
    and $\overline G_{\ell}^\star(n,\cdot) :=G_{\ell}(n,\cdot) \star \overline \Pi(n-1,\cdot)$.

[Lemma tiltlemma6.4 of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] Take $B>0$, $\zeta\in\Gamma_B$ and $X\sim\operatorname{Col}_n(\zeta)$. Then we can find some $c\in(0,1)$ depending only on $B$ so that for any $u,v\in\mathbb{R}^n$,\begin{equation}
        |\mathbb{E}_Xe^{2\pi i\langle X,v\rangle+\langle X,u\rangle}|\leq \exp(-c\min_{r\in[1,c^{-1}]}\|rv\|_\mathbb{T}^2+c^{-1}\|u\|_2^2).
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

