[Lem lem-time-finite of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] There exists a function $\mathfrak w_* : \mathcal V\mathcal G\to (0,\infty)$ such that if $\mathfrak w(x) \geq \mathfrak w_*(x)$ for all but finitely many $x \in \mathcal V\mathcal G$, then the following is true. 
For each choice of starting point $z\in\mathcal V\mathcal G$, it holds $\mathbbm P_z$-a.s.\ that 
\begin{equation}  
\sum_{\xi \in \Xi} T_\xi= \infty  \quad \text{and} \quad \sum_{\xi \in\Xi , \xi\leq \eta} T_\xi < \infty ,\quad \forall \eta\in\Xi  .
\end{equation}

