[Proposition 39 of arXiv:2609.00567, 'Hodge--Tate splitting and Akizuki--Nakano vanishing in positive characteristic'] Let \(k\) be a perfect field of characteristic \(p\) and let \(T\) be an algebraic fpqc \(k\)-stack.
  Assume that \(T\) admits an algebraic fpqc \(W(k)\)-\(\delta\)-lifting \(\widetilde T\), together with an isomorphism $\widetilde T_{\F_p}\simeq T$.
  Then there exists a morphism
  \begin{equation*}
    s' \colon WT_{\setF_p} \to T
  \end{equation*}
  and a commutative diagram
  \begin{equation*}
    \begin{tikzcd}
    WT_{\setF_p} \arrow[d, "s'"'] \arrow[rd, "\sigma_{T}"] &         \\
    T \arrow[r, "\pi_T"']                                  & T^{\dR}
    \end{tikzcd}
  \end{equation*}
  of \(\setF_p\)-stacks, where \(\sigma_T\) is the morphism constructed in \Cref{ConstPetrov}.

