{"artifact_digest":"sha256:c26fa76f4f46f6ec29c94f1a5cf249669d05da7e6e95d83868377d57307868fa","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/c2/c26fa76f4f46f6ec29c94f1a5cf249669d05da7e6e95d83868377d57307868fa.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:93a49fbc7c7ec719e54e0f8367135b51ccfa4faf0997f634efdabdb4e07cc572","bundle_entry_key":"2609-03726-lemma-8-farfield-expansion","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_163","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_163.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2609-03726-lemma-8-farfield-expansion","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: By \eqref{eq:sc_equation} and \eqref{eq:total_field}, the scattered field
satisfies
\begin{equation*}
    P_k^0\,\psi^{\mathrm{sc}}_{k,\alpha}
    =
    -V_k\psi^{\mathrm{in}}_{k,\alpha}-V_k\psi^{\mathrm{sc}}_{k,\alpha}
    =
    -V_k\,\psi_{k,\alpha}.
\end{equation*}
Since $\psi^{\mathrm{sc}}_{k,\alpha}$ is outgoing, we have
\begin{equation*}
    \psi^{\mathrm{sc}}_{k,\alpha}
    =
    -R_k^0 h,
\end{equation*}
where $h = V_k\,\psi_{k,\alpha}$ is a compactly supported function.

