body:
[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2606.06757, 'Path-Dependent Ergodic Optimal Control \\ and Backward Stochastic Differential Equations'] Let $(a_n)_{n\ge1}$ be a sequence in $\mathbb{R}$ satisfying $\sup_{m,n\ge 1}
|a_{n+m}-a_n-a_m|<\infty$.
Then there exists $\lambda\in\mathbb{R}$ such that $\sup_{n\ge1}|a_n-\lambda n|<\infty$. In particular, $\frac{a_n}{n}\xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{}\lambda$.

[Definition def:trel of arXiv:2508.21055, 'Modern aspects of Markov chains:\\entropy, curvature and the cutoff phenomenon'] There is a number $\lambda>0$, called the \red[spectral gap], such that
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item ${\rm d}_{\textsc{tv}}(t) = \exp\left(-\lambda t+o(t)\right)$ as $t\to +\infty$;
\item ${\rm d}_{\textsc{tv}}(t) \ge \frac{1}{2}\exp\left(-\lambda t\right)$, for all $t\ge 0$.
\end{enumerate}

[Theorem 32 of arXiv:2608.26816, '\textbf{On the existence of maximal foliations in general relativity}'] Under the assumptions of Theorem \ref{maxfol}, if the following holds at time $t=0$ for some $k\geq 2$:   
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{i=0}^{k}||\nabla^i \bar{R}m||^2_{L^2(M_0)}+\sum_{i=1}^{k+1}||\nabla^i h ||^2_{L^2(M_0)}< \infty,
\end{equation}

then there exists  $\Lambda_k>0$ depending only  on the initial data $(g_0,h_0)$ such that   for any $t>0$, we have 
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
 \sum_{i=0}^{k}||\nabla^i \bar{R}m||^2_{L^2(M_t)}+\sum_{i=1}^{k+1}||\nabla^i h ||^2_{L^2(M_t)} \leq \Lambda_k.
 \end{split}
 \end{equation}

