[Proposition 28 (decay of the $A$-tensor and of the base curvature) of arXiv:2609.03332, 'Singularity Models of Finite-Time K\"ahler-Ricci Flows'] Let $A$ denote the O'Neill tensor of the extended submersion $\widehat{\pi} : \widehat{M} \to N$ of \S\ref{subsec:oneill} (including its symmetric part, i.e. the full second fundamental form of the splitting $T\widehat{M} = \mathcal{V} \oplus \mathcal{H}$; recall $T \equiv 0$ by Proposition \ref{prop:2.5}). Then there is $C = C ( g_0, T )$ with

	\begin{equation}
		\big| A \big|^2_{g(t)} \;\leq\; \frac{C}{T - t} \qquad \text{on } \widehat{M} \times [0, T) \,,
	\end{equation}

	and the same bound holds for the sectional curvatures of horizontal planes of $g(t)$ and for those of the evolving base metric $\check{g}_t = \sum_i f_i^2\, g_i$. Consequently, along the Type II rescaling,

	\begin{equation}
		\big| A \big|^2_{g_j(t)} \;=\; K_j^{-1}\, \big| A \big|^2_{g ( t_j + K_j^{-1} t )} \;\leq\; \frac{C}{K_j ( T - t_j ) - t} \;\longrightarrow\; 0 \qquad ( j \to \infty ) \,,
	\end{equation}

	locally uniformly in $t \in \mathbb{R}$, and likewise for the rescaled horizontal and base sectional curvatures: a Type II blow-up sees a flat base and an integrable, totally geodesic horizontal distribution. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem 33 of arXiv:2510.26216, 'A functional Breuer-Major theorem with Poisson noise'] For every $\ell\in\NN$, every $\vec{r}\in\NN^\ell$, we have 
    \begin{equation*}
        \sup_{n\ge 1}|\d^{\vec{r}}_{\vec{\theta}}\bB_{n,\ell}(\vec{\theta})|+|\d^{\vec{r}}_{\vec{\theta}}\widetilde{\bB}_{\ell}(\vec{\theta})|\lesssim \prod_{q=1}^\ell(1+|\theta_q|)^{d_\alpha},
    \end{equation*}
    where the proportionality constant is independent of $\vec{\theta}\in\RR^\ell$.

