body:
[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2609.02478, 'Improved Weyl bounds on short intervals'] Under the hypotheses of \cref{prop:orbit-collision}, let $x\ne y$ satisfy \eqref{eq:centre-collision}, and put $h=x-y$.  Then, if $\delta=\delta(k)$ is sufficiently small, there are integers $r,v_2,\ldots,v_k$ such that
\begin{equation}
  1\le r\le N,
  \qquad
  \gcd(r,v_2,\ldots,v_k)=1,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
  |r\alpha_j-v_j|
  \le\frac{N^{1-j}}{4k^4}
  \qquad(2\le j\le k).
\end{equation}

