[Lemma lem:stat_obeys_slope of arXiv:2605.22787, 'Invariant measures for half-space geometric LPP: classification and the one force--one sol'] Assume that $s \ge r_c$, but $s \neq 1$. Let $(f_n)_{n \ge 1}$ be any sequence of functions $\mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{R}$ such that $f_n \sim \mu_{c,s}$ for all $n \ge 1$. Set $\theta = T_c(s)$. Then, with probability one,
    \begin{equation} 
    \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{1}{n} \max_{k \in \llbracket 1,n \rrbracket}[|f_n(k) -\theta k|] = 0.
    \end{equation}
    In particular, for each $\xi \in [0,1]$, we have 
    \begin{equation} 
    \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{f_n(1 +\lfloor \xi n \rfloor)}{n} = \theta\xi.
    \end{equation}

