[Lemma 28 (Fractional-covering duality) of arXiv:2606.07931, 'Pointwise Complexity for Gaussian Fields:\\Upper Envelopes, Algorithmic Lower Bounds, and '] For a finite metric space \((T,d)\) and any \(\Delta>0\),
\begin{equation}
N_{\rm frac}(T,d,\Delta)
:=
\inf_{\mu\in\Delta(T)}\sup_{x\in T}\frac{1}{\mu(B_d(x,\Delta))}
=
\sup_{\pi\in\Delta(T)}\frac{1}{\sup_{a\in T}\pi(B_d(a,\Delta))}.
\end{equation}

