body:
[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2604.19924, 'Fluctuation theory for spectrally negative Lévy processes killed by additive functionals'] For any $T>y$
				, a locally bounded function $h:\R\to\R$, and two Radon measures $\nu$ and $\lambda$ such that 
				\begin{align}
					\inf_{x\in[y,T]}(1-W^{(q)}(0)(\nu-\lambda)\{x\})>0,
				\end{align}
				the equation
				\begin{align}
					H(x,y)= h(x-y)+\int_{[y,x]}W^{(q)}(x-z)H(z,y)(\nu-\lambda)(dz),\qquad x\in\R.
				\end{align}
				admits a unique locally bounded solution {$H(x, y)=H_{\nu-\lambda}^{(q)}(x, y)$} on $[y,T]$. Furthermore, if $h(x)\geq0$ for all $x\in[y,T]$ and $\nu-\lambda$ is a non-negative measure, then $H(x,y)\geq0$ for all $x\in[y,T]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:smoothedlower of arXiv:2606.11248, 'Persistent Homology of the Planar Wiener Sausage: Brownian Scaling and a Logarithmic Expec'] Let $\psi\ge0$ be bounded and supported in $[r_{0},r_{1}]\subset(0,\infty)$. Then
\begin{equation}
\liminf_{T\to\infty}\frac{\mathbb{E}[\Phi_{\psi}(T)]}{T/(\log T)^{2}}\ge c_{-}\int_{r_{0}}^{r_{1}}\frac{\psi(r)}{r^{2}}\,dr.
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:largesingkeloop of arXiv:2508.09291, '1+O(1) asymptotics for loop percolation in five and higher dimensions'] Suppose $d\ge 3$. As $m\to\infty$ and for $\left| x \right|=o(m)$
    \begin{equation}
        \mu\ek{\omega\colon 0\longleftrightarrow x\textnormal{ and }\mathrm{diam}(\omega)>m}={\mathcal O }\rk{m^{2-d}\left| x \right|^{2-d}}\, .
    \end{equation}

