[Thm exact_Wa of arXiv:2604.07183, 'Stopping on the last success with unknown odds: asymptotic minimax optimality of the plug-'] Let~$a\in(0,1)$ and~$n\ge2$ be such that~$1\le t_a\le n-1$, and let~$\ell_j$ be as in~((eq:La_def of the paper)). Then, for any~$p\in(0,1)$,
\begin{equation}
W_n^{\pi_a}(p)
=
\sum_{j=0}^{t_a}
\binom{t_a}{j}p^j(1-p)^{t_a-j}
\ell_jp(1-p)^{\ell_j-1}
.
\end{equation}
In particular, $p\mapsto W_n^{\pi_a}(p)$ is a polynomial and can be evaluated in~$O(n)$ arithmetic operations.

