[Lemma lem:de l'orangeraie of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Recall that we denote by $b_m$, respectively $s_m$ the $m$-dimensional volume of the Euclidean unit ball $B\subset\mathbb{R}^m$, respectively unit sphere $S^m\subset \mathbb{R}^{m+1}$. We have:
  \begin{equation}
    \frac{m! b_m s_m}{(2\pi)^m}=2.
  \end{equation}

