[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2604.07697, 'Stochastic fractional heat equation with general rough noise'] Assume $0<H<\frac12$ and $1<\alpha<2$. Denote $\lambda(x)=\frac{1}{(1+|x|^2)^{1-H}}$.  We have
\begin{align} 
&\int_{\mathbb{R}^2}\left|D(t,x,h)\right|^2|h|^{2H-2}\lambda(z-x)dxdh\le c_{T,H,\alpha}t^{\frac{2(H-1)}{\alpha}}\lambda(z), \\
&\int_{\mathbb{R}^3}\left|\Box(t,x,y,h)\right|^2|h|^{2H-2}|y|^{2H-2}\lambda(z-x)dxdydh\le c_{T,H,\alpha}t^{\frac{4H-3}{\alpha}}\lambda(z). 
\end{align}

