[Prop 26 of arXiv:2606.24887, '2606.24887'] We fix constants $L >0$ and $0 < \delta <1 $. Then there exists a constant $\mathcal{C} >0$ depending only on $L$ and $\delta$ such that for any $N^{-1+ \delta} \le \eta_{\ast} < \eta^{\ast} \le L$, if $\widetilde{\Delta}(\eta^*) \leq \mathcal C \widetilde{\psi}_w(\eta^*)$ with very high probability, then the event 
		\begin{equation*}
			\left\{  \widetilde{\Lambda}(\eta)\le \mathcal{C} \widetilde{\psi}_w(\eta)  ~~\text{for all}~ \eta \in [ \eta_{\ast}, \eta^{\ast}] \right\}
		\end{equation*}
		holds with very high probability on the event $\{ \theta =1 ~\text{for all} ~ \eta \in [\eta_{\ast}, \eta^{\ast}]\}$ 
		uniformly for $w \in \mathrm{D}_2$.

