[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2608.29361, 'Convergence of the subcritical $\gamma$-LQG metric to the critical $2$-LQG metric as $\gam'] (\cite[Lemma~3.3]{kavvadias2025continuity})

For each $M>0$, there exists $\mathfrak{p}_0 \in (0,1)$ depending only on $M$ such that the following holds for all $\mathfrak{p} \in (\mathfrak{p}_0,1)$. Let $\{E_r(z)\}_{z \in \CC,r>0}$ be a collection of events such that for all $z \in \CC,r>0$, we have that $\mathbb{P}[E_r(z)] = \mathbb{P}[E_1(0)] \geq \mathfrak{p}$ and $E_r(z)$ is measurable with respect to the $\sigma$-algebra generated by 
\begin{equation*}
    (h-h_{3r}(z))|_{\mathbb{A}_{r,2r}(z)}.
\end{equation*}
Then, for all $\mathfrak{r}>0$, it holds with probability at least $1 - \varepsilon^M$ as $\varepsilon \to 0$, at a rate which is universal, that the following is true. For each $z \in B_{\mathfrak{r} \varepsilon^{-M}}(0)$, there exist 
\begin{equation*}
    r \in [\varepsilon^2 \mathfrak{r},\varepsilon \mathfrak{r}] \cap \{2^{-k} \mathfrak{r}\}_{k \in \NN}, w \in B_{\mathfrak{r} \varepsilon^{-M}}(0) \cap \left(\frac{\varepsilon^2 \mathfrak{r}}{4} \ZZ^2\right)
\end{equation*}
such that $E_r(w)$ occurs and $z \in B_{\mathfrak{r} \varepsilon^2 / 2}(w)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem 33 (Exact evaluation of $\mathcal{U}$) of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] Write $a_0 \coloneqq (2\log 2 - 1)/\left((1 - \log 2)\sqrt{2\log 2}\right)$. The function $\mathcal{U}$ of \eqref{eqn:sgM} is given by
\begin{align}
    \mathcal{U}(a) =
    \begin{cases}
        a\log 2 + \sqrt{2\log 2}, & 0 < a \le a_0,\\[2mm]
        \displaystyle a + \frac{1}{ad_0 + \sqrt{a^2d_0^2 + 2d_0}}, & a \ge a_0.
    \end{cases}

\end{align}

