[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2608.28964, '2608.28964'] For any $\gamma>0$, there exists a constant $C_\gamma>0$ such that for any $t\geq s\geq0$ and $V_s\in \mathcal X$, the solution $(v,p)=\mathcal J_{s,\cdot}V_s$ of \eqref{eq J} satisfies
	\begin{align}
	\sup_{s\leq r\leq t}\|\mathcal J_{s,r}V_s\|_{\mathcal X}^2+\int_s^t\left(\|v_r\|_{\mathcal H^2}^2+\|\nabla p_r\|^2\right)dr\leq C_\gamma\exp\left(\gamma\int_s^t\|u_r\|_{\mathcal H^2}^2dr+C_\gamma(t-s)\right)\|V_s\|_{\mathcal X}^2.
	\end{align}

