[Definition def-transport-weak-2 of arXiv:2512.17727, 'Stochastic transport equation with L\'evy noise'] A weak$^\ast$-$\mathrm{L}^{\infty}$-solution to the stochastic transport equation
(equation eqn-transport-strong of the paper)  is
\begin{trivlist}
\item[(o)] a measurable and essentially bounded function
\begin{equation}
u:
[0,T]\times\mathbb{R}^d\times \Omega \to \mathbb{R}
\end{equation}
\end{trivlist}
{
in the sense  that there exists $M>0 $ satisfying
  \begin{align}
    \sup_{t\in[0,T]}\| u(t, \cdot, \omega) \|_{L^\infty(\mathbb{R}^d)} \leq M,\quad\mathbb{P}\text{-a.s.}
\end{align}
}
together with the following two additional conditions
\begin{trivlist}
\item[(i)] for every test function  $\theta\in C_c^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^d)$, the process $u_t(\theta)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}\theta(x)u(t,x)\,dx$, $t\in [0,T]$ is  $\mathbb{F}$-adapted and it has   c\`{a}dl\`{a}g paths, $\mathbb{P}$-a.s.;
\item[(ii)] for every test function  $\theta\in C_c^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^d)$, the process $\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}\theta(x)u(t,x)\,dx$,  $t\in [0,T]$,  satisfies that, for every $t\in [0,T]$, $\mathbb{P}$-a.s.,
\begin{align}
      &\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}u(t,x)\,\theta(x)\,dx\\
   & =
    \int_{\mathbb{R}^d}u_{0}(x)\,\theta(x)\,dx
       +\int_0^t\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}u(s,x)\,[b(x)\cdot  D\theta(x)+\operatorname{div}\, b(x)\,\theta(x)]\,dx\,ds\\
       &\quad +\int_0^t\Xint\times_{B} \Bigl(\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}u(s-,x)\,[\theta(x+z)-\theta(x)]\, dx\Bigr)\tilde{\mu}(ds,dz)\\
       &\quad+\int_0^t\int_{B^{\mathrm{c}}} \Bigl(\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}u(s-,x)\,[\theta(x+z)-\theta(x)]\, dx\Bigr) \mu(ds,dz)\\
       &\quad+\int_0^t\Xint\times_{B}\Bigl(\int_{\mathbb{R}^d} u(s,x)\,[\theta(x+z)-\theta(x)-\sum_{i=1}^dz_iD_i\theta(x)]\,dx\Bigr)\,\nu(dz)\, ds.
\end{align}
The $\mathbb{P}$-a.s. means as usual that we have a 
$\mathbb{P}$-full  set involved. 
Actually, one could make this $\mathbb{P}$-full set independent of $t$ and $\theta$ by Lemma (lem-transport-weak-2-(i) of the paper).
\end{trivlist}

[Corollary eq:eq norm of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Assume that $d\ge 3$, $s\in (1,d/2)$ and $\alpha\in (0,1)$ and $\alpha\in (0,1/2)$, let $M_0$ be in $\dot{H}^{-s}$, fix $R>0$. Let $M$ be a solution to (equation eq:KK of the paper) (in the sense of (def:sol of the paper)) which is also in $L^2_{t,\omega}(\dot{H}^{-s+1-\alpha})$. Then we have
