[Proposition prop: BK-prob of arXiv:2411.07840, 'Central limit theorem for the focusing $Φ^4$-measure in the infinite volume limit'] There are constants $C$, $c>0$ such that, for $K$ large enough, we have 
\begin{align}
\nu^\perp_{Q, x_0}(B_K^c) \le C e^{-cK^2 \log L^2},

\end{align}

\noindent
uniformly in $x_0 \in \mathbb{T}_{L^2}$ and $\theta \in [0,2\pi]$, where $B_K=\{\|h^\perp \|_{L^\infty(\mathbb{T}_{L^2})  } \le K \sqrt{\log L^2}  \}$ was introduced in (equation eqn: BK-def of the paper).

