body:
[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2608.25706, 'Fast rates in Bayesian online learning with approximate posteriors'] Under \cref{ass:sequence_model}, there is an absolute constant $L_{\cM}>0$ such that
    \begin{align*}
    \cM_t(Q)-\cM_t(P)
    \le L_{\cM}\cbr{  \Wp(P,\delta_{\theta^\star})\Wp(P,Q)+\Wp^2(P,Q) }
\end{align*}
almost surely for every $t\in\bN$ and for any two product measures $P=\bigotimes_{j\ge 1}P_j$ and $Q=\bigotimes_{j\ge 1}Q_j$ on $\prod_{j\ge 1}[-B,B]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

