body:
[Lemma LM42 of arXiv:2412.08886, 'On domination for (non-symmetric) Dirichlet forms'] The right process $X^G$ is $m|_{G}$-tight and is properly associated with the quasi-regular Dirichlet form given by
\begin{equation}
	\begin{aligned}
		&{\mathscr F}^G:=\{f\in {\mathscr F}: \tilde{f}=0,{\mathscr E}\text{-q.e. on }B\},\\
		&{\mathscr E}^G(f,g):={\mathscr E}(f,g),\quad f,g\in {\mathscr F}^G
	\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
on $L^2(G,m|_G)$,  where $\tilde{f}$ denotes the ${\mathscr E}$-quasi-continuous $m$-version of $f$.

