body:
[Lemma linearity of arXiv:2608.21805, 'Logarithmic derivatives of variational and singular stochastic partial differential equati'] The random field $w_r(z) = \Phi_r^{*}\,z$ is linear in $z$, and its Fr\'echet derivative is
\begin{equation}
  \nabla_z w_r = \Phi_r^{*} \in L_2(H, U),
\end{equation}
which is independent of $z$.

