[Lem lm5 of arXiv:2411.01849, 'A tamed-adaptive Milstein scheme for stochastic differential equations with low regularity'] For any $p>0$, there exists a positive constant $C_p$ which does not depend on $\Delta$ such that, for any $t>0$, 
\begin{itemize}
\item[\textnormal{i)}] $\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\widehat{X}_t- \widehat{X}_{\underline{t}}\right|^p \Big| \mathcal{F}_{\underline{t}}\right] \leq C_p \Delta^{p/2},$
\item[\textnormal{ii)}]$\mathbb{E}\left[\left|\widehat{X}_t- \widehat{X}_{\underline{t}}- \sigma(\widehat{X}_{\underline{t}})(W_t- W_{\underline{t}})\right|^p \Big| \mathcal{F}_{\underline{t}}\right] \leq C_p \Delta^{p}.$
\end{itemize}

