[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2609.02801, 'Ratio and limiting zero distribution asymptotics for symmetric multiple orthogonal polynom'] Suppose $(a_n)_{n\geq 0}$ is a positive sequence for which
\begin{equation}  
    a_{n+1} \leq c_n + a \sum_{k=0}^{r-1} a_{n-k}, \qquad  n \geq 0, 
\end{equation}    
where $r$ is an integer $\geq 1$, $0 < a \leq 1$ and $(c_n)_{n \geq 0}$ a positive sequence. Then one has
\begin{equation}  
     a_{n+1} \leq   a_0 A^{n+1} + \sum_{k=0}^n c_k A^{n-k}, 
\end{equation}
where $A = 2 a^{1/r}$.

