[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2608.12291, 'When should one stop the most exciting game?\\ {\tiny Sequential Inference for win-marting'] If Assumption \ref{asmp:baseline} and $T\leq \infty$ hold, then $V_T$ is upper semicontinuous, $\mathcal{C}_T$ is open, and $\mathcal{D}_T$ is closed. Furthermore, the stopping time
\begin{equation}
    \tau^*_T(t,x):=\inf\{0\le s<T-t:(t+s,X_s^x)\in\mathcal{D}_T\}\wedge(T-t)
\end{equation}
is the smallest optimal stopping time for $T<\infty$.

