[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2512.07202, 'Hitting Probabilities for Hypoelliptic Differential Equations Driven by Fractional Brownia'] There exist a constant $C > 0$ and a family of positive random variables $(\Psi^1_{s,t})_{0 \leqslant s < t}$, where the Malliavin-Sobolev norm of each $\Psi^1_{s,t}$ does not depend on $s$ or $t$, such that
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\left( \mathbf{U}_{s,t} \geqslant u \,\middle|\, \mathcal{F}_s^W \right) \leqslant \exp\left(-\frac{\|u\|_{\mathrm{CC}}^2}{C(t-s)^{2H}}\right) \Psi^1_{s,t}
\end{equation}
for all $u \in \mathfrak{g}^{(l)}$ and $0\leqslant s<t\leqslant T$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:ExpGSA of arXiv:2605.05193, 'Grokability in five inequalities'] Fix $n\ge 1$, $\rho>0$, and an integer $N\ge 1$.
Let $x_1,\dots,x_N$ be i.i.d.\ uniform on the unit sphere $S^n\subset\mathbb{R}^{n+1}$ and set
\[
Q:=\bigcap_{j=1}^N\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{n+1}:\ \langle x,x_j\rangle\le \rho\}.
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}\,\operatorname{GSA}(Q)
=
N\,\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-\rho^2/2}
\int_{\mathbb{R}^n}\varphi_n(y)\,\bigl(1-p(|y|)\bigr)^{N-1}\,dy,
\end{equation}
where $p(r)$ depends only on $r\ge 0$ and is given by
\begin{equation}
p(r)=
\Bigg(\int_{-\sqrt{r^2+\rho^2}}^{\sqrt{r^2+\rho^2}}
\Bigl(1-\frac{t^2}{r^2+\rho^2}\Bigr)^{\frac{n-2}{2}}\,dt\Bigg)^{-1}
\int_{\rho}^{\sqrt{r^2+\rho^2}}
\Bigl(1-\frac{t^2}{r^2+\rho^2}\Bigr)^{\frac{n-2}{2}}\,dt .
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2604.15226, '\bfseries Nonlinear Schrödinger equations with spatial white noise potential on full space'] Let $0<\mu\le1$. For any initial data $u_0\in \CD_\mu^1$, there exists energy solutions in $\CC(\IR,\CD_\mu^1)$ to \eqref{NLS} on $\IR^3$ for $1\le m<6$. For any time interval $I$ containing $0$, we have the bound
\begin{equation}
\sup_{t\in I}\|u(t)\|_{\CD_\mu^1}\lesssim(1+|I|)\|u_0\|_{\CD_\mu^1}
\end{equation}
with a constant that depends only on the noise. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2603.27712, 'Bridging Schr\"odinger and Bass: A Semimartingale Optimal Transport Problem with Diffusion'] We have
\begin{equation}
\Vc(\mu_0,\mu_T)
= \underline{\Vc}(\mu_0,\mu_T)
:= \sup_{\psi\in\Cc_{w,\uparrow}^{\conc}}
\{\mu_T(\psi)-\mu_0(V_0^\psi)\}.
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
\mu_T(\psi)-\mu_0(V_0^\psi)
\le \Vc(\mu_0,\mu_T), ~~\mbox{for all}~~ \psi\in\Cc^{\conc},
\end{equation}
where the objective is understood in the extended sense. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

