body:
[Lemma lem:closure of arXiv:2606.24881, 'Queues with Correlated Service Times --- the $M/M_D/c$ Model'] Let $\mathbf{X} = (X_1, \ldots, X_c)$ be a random vector following MO-MVED with survival function given in (equation eqn:MO-MVE of the paper).
Then, for any nonempty subset \( T \subseteq \{1,\ldots,c\} \), the marginal vector \( X_T = (X_i)_{i \in T} \) has its survival function \( \bar{H}_T(\mathbf{x}_T) = \mathbb{P}(X_i > x_i, \forall i \in T) \) given by
\begin{equation}
\bar{H}_T(\mathbf{x}_T) = \exp\left( - \sum_{\forall A : A \cap T \neq \emptyset} \mu_A \max_{i \in A \cap T} x_i \right),
\end{equation}
where \(\mathbf{x}_T=(x_i)_{i \in T} \). Notice that if we denote $\mathcal{P}_T := 2^T \setminus \emptyset$, which is the power set of $T$ excluding the empty set, then $\mathcal{P}_T = \{ B \subset T: B= A \cap T \text{ with } A \subseteq \{1, 2, \ldots, c \}\setminus \emptyset \}$. Therefore, \( \bar{H}_T \) can be expressed as
\begin{equation}
  \bar{H}_T(\mathbf{x}_T) = \exp\left( - \sum_{\forall B \subseteq \mathcal{P}_T} \mu_B^{T} \max_{i \in B} x_i \right),
\end{equation}
where \( \mu_B^{T} \) is the shock rate associated with subset $B$ of components in the marginal distribution of \( X_T \), given by
\begin{equation} 
  \mu_B^{T} = \sum_{A : A \cap T = B \neq \emptyset} \mu_A.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma Lemma-immersioni of arXiv:2512.17736, 'Pathwise uniqueness by noise for singular stochastic PDEs'] Let $\eta\in\left[\frac14,\frac12\right]$
and $\sigma\geq \frac12-\eta$ be such that $2\eta+\sigma>\frac{d+2}{4}$. Then, for every $f\in V_{2\eta}$ and $g\in V_{2\eta-1}$, 
the product $fg$ is well-defined as an element of 
$V_{-2\sigma}$, and
there exists a positive constant $C$ such that 
\begin{align}
\|fg\|_{V_{-2\sigma}}\leq C\|f\|_{V_{2\eta}}\|g\|_{V_{2\eta-1}}
\qquad   \forall\,f\in V_{2\eta}\,,\quad\forall\, g\in V_{2\eta-1}\,.  
\end{align}

