[Lemma lemma-5.7 of arXiv:2412.08964, 'Phase transition and critical behavior in hierarchical\\integer-valued Gaussian and Coulom'] For all~$\alpha\in(-\ffrac12,\ffrac12)$ and~$\delta\in(0,1-2|\alpha|)$ there exist~$\epsilon>0$ and $C'>0$ and, for all~$\beta>\beta_\text{\rm c}$ with~$1/\beta>1/\beta_\text{\rm c}-\epsilon$, there exist $C>0$  and  $\eta>0$ such that
\begin{equation}

\Gamma^\star_j(p)\le C'\sqrt{b\theta-1}\,\,\,b^{-(1-2|\alpha|-\delta)j}\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{-\eta|p|(|p|-1)}
\end{equation}
holds for all~$j\ge2$ and $p\in\mathbb Z$ and
\begin{equation}

\bigl|\Gamma_{k,j}(p,0)-\Gamma^\star_j(p)\bigr|\le Cb^{-(1-2|\alpha|-\delta)j}\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{-\eta|p|(|p|-1)}\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{-\eta \min\{k,n-k\}}
\end{equation}
holds for $n\ge k> j\ge1$ and~$p\in\mathbb Z$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

