|x^{k_{i,j}}|=|\lambda_i|
\end{equation*}
($j \in [1, n_i],\  i \in [1,n]$).

[Lemma 10 (Binomial collision kernel) of arXiv:2607.04467, 'Bernstein Functions at Work:\\ Coalescents, Copulas, and Subordination'] For every integer $n\ge2$ and $x,y\ge0$ with $x+y\le1$,
\begin{equation}
(1-x)^n+(1-y)^n-1-(1-x-y)^n
=-\,n(n-1)\int_0^x\!\!\int_0^y(1-r-t)^{n-2}\,dr\,dt,
\end{equation}
and $\;1-(1-x)^n=n\int_0^x(1-t)^{n-1}\,dt$.

