[Lem maximal-vertical-oscillations-with-floor of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] Consider a $2N\times 2N$ box with boundary conditions that are $+$ on the bottom side, and $-$ on the other three sides, for $N\ge e^{\beta/5}$. There exists a $C$ (independent of $\beta$) such that for all $\beta>\beta_0$, for all $h$, 
        \begin{align*}
            \pi^{(-,-,+,-)}(\lambda(\sigma) \text{ reaches $H_h^*$}) \le C N^C \exp( - \kappa_\beta (\tfrac{h^2}{b-a-1} \wedge h))\,.
        \end{align*}

[Lemma of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] The global $J$-homomorphism ${\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak J}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{gl}^\otimes\colon\ul\textup{VRep}^{\oplus}\to{\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{gl}^\otimes$ factors uniquely through a symmetric monoidal $\textup{Glo}$-functor $\smash{{\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak J}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}^\otimes\colon\ul\textup{VRep}^{\oplus}\to{\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}^\otimes}$.
    \begin{proof}
        By Proposition~(prop:mySp-vs-mySp-gl of the paper), the unique equivariantly cocontinuous symmetric monoidal global functor $i\colon {\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}^\otimes\to{\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{gl}^\otimes$ is fully faithful and at every compact Lie group $G$, it admits a right adjoint $r_G\colon{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_{\text{$G$-gl}}^{\otimes}\to {\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_{G}^{\otimes}$ which is a localization at the equivariant weak equivalences.
        As equivariant weak equivalences are preserved by smashing with flat orthogonal $G$-spectra (Theorem~(thm:equiv-flatness of the paper)), it follows that the induced lax symmetric monoidal structure on the right adjoint $r_G$ is strong. 
        By [puetzstueck-new]*{Corollary 6.3}, this implies that $\smash{i_G\colon \Sp_G^{\otimes}\rightleftarrows \Sp_{\text{$G$-gl}}^{\otimes}
	\nobreak
	\mspace{6mu plus 1mu}
	{:}
	\nonscript\mkern-\thinmuskip
	\mathpunct{}
	\mspace{2mu}
 r_G}$ induce mutually inverse equivalences 
        $\smash{\textup{pic}(\Sp_G^{\otimes})\simeq \textup{pic}(\Sp_\text{$G$-gl}^{\otimes})}$ for all compact Lie groups $G$.  
        In particular, $i$ restricts to an equivalence $\smash{\textup{pic}({\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}^{\otimes})\xrightarrow{\;\smash{\raisebox{-0.25ex}{\ensuremath{\scriptstyle\sim}}}\;} \textup{pic}({\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_{\textup{gl}}^{\otimes})}$, so that ${\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak J}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{gl}^\otimes$ factors uniquely through ${\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}^\otimes$ as claimed.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:results:uniqueRegime of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Suppose $(U, W)$ satisfy Assumption (as:results:fixedPoint of the paper) and Assumption (as:results:LSI of the paper). Then there exists a unique Cayley fixed point $\pi \in \tilde{\mathcal{M}}_{2, d}$ and we have $\mathbb H_2^* = \mathbb H_2(\pi)$. In other words, for $\mathcal{Z}^n$ as in (equation eq:results:gibbsPFN of the paper), we have
\begin{equation*}
    \lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{2n+1} \log \mathcal{Z}^n = \mathbb H_2(\pi).
\end{equation*}
Furthermore, we have \begin{equation}
        \mathbb H_2(\nu) - \mathbb H_2(\pi) = \mathcal{H}(\nu|\pi) - \mathcal{H}(\bar{\nu}|\bar{\pi}), \quad \nu \in \mathcal{Q}_{2, d}.

    \end{equation}
Moreover, if there exists a solution to the 2-MLFE with potentials $(U, W)$ and initial distribution $\pi$, then $\pi$ is the unique stationary distribution of the 2-MLFE in the sense of Definition (def:results:stationary of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:final v inequality of arXiv:2512.12902, 'Non-equilibrium fluctuations for the \\stirring process with births and deaths'] Let  $2\leq K\leq N$ be a fixed  integer number  and   $\zeta>0$. Let also  
 $\mu^{\epsilon}$  be any initial measure satisfying (equation Ass1 of the paper),   $0<t\leq T$ and  $2\leq n\leq N^*-1$, where $N^*$ is defined in (equation N* of the paper). Then, the following bound holds:
\begin{eqnarray}
&&\hspace{-0.5cm}|v_n^{\epsilon}(\underline{x},t)|\lesssim \mathbf 1_{n=2,3}\epsilon T^{1/2}+\mathbf 1_{4\leq n\leq N^*-1}\epsilon^{1+\zeta}T^{1/2}\nonumber\\ 
&&\hspace{1cm}+\int_{0}^t d\lambda \;\epsilon^{-1}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\sum_{z'\in I_{+}} \mathbf 1_{n\leq N^*-1}\mathbf{E}_\epsilon \left[\mathbf{1}_{x_j(\lambda)\in I_+} |v_{n}^\epsilon\left(\underline{x}^{(j)}(\lambda)\cup z',t-\lambda\right)|\Big]\right]\nonumber\\
&&\hspace{1cm}+\int_{0}^t d\lambda \;\frac{\epsilon^{-1}}{[\epsilon^{-2}\lambda]^{1/2}+1}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\sum_{\underline{z}'\subset I_{+},q\geq 2} \mathbf 1_{n+q\leq N^*-1}\mathbf{E}_\epsilon \left[ |v_{n-1+q}^\epsilon\big(\underline{x}^{(j)}(\lambda)\cup\underline{z}',t-\lambda\big)|\Big]\right]\nonumber\\
&&\hspace{1cm}+\int_{0}^t d\lambda \;
\epsilon^{-1}\mathbf{E}_\epsilon \left[ {\bf 1}_{\underline{x}(\lambda)=I^n_+}\right].
\end{eqnarray}

