body:
[Proposition prop:feature-edge of arXiv:2608.10184, 'The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase transition in random ellipsoid fitting'] Let $K \subset (0, 1/2)$ be compact and let $n = n(p)$ satisfy $n/p^2 \in K$ for all large $p$.  There are constants $0 < c_K \le C_K < \infty$ such that, with probability tending to one as $p \to \infty$,
\begin{equation}
c_K\, p^2\, I_d_n \;\preceq\; \mathcal{Q}_y \mathcal{Q}_y^* \;\preceq\; C_K\, p^2\, I_d_n .
\end{equation}
In particular, with probability tending to one,
\begin{equation}
\sup_{T \neq 0} \frac{\|\mathcal{Q}_y(T)\|_2}{\sqrt n\, \|T\|_{\mathrm{F}}} \le C_K' .
\end{equation}
Moreover, if $\mathcal{G}(T) = (\sqrt p \operatorname{Tr}(G_i T))_{i=1}^n$ with $G_i \stackrel{\mathrm{iid}}{\sim} \operatorname{GOE}(p)$, then $\|\mathcal{G}\|_{\mathrm{F} \to 2} \le C_K' \sqrt n$ with probability at least $1 - 2e^{-n/2}$.  All constants and all $o(1)$ probabilities are uniform over sequences with $n/p^2 \in K$.

