[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2609.03726, 'Inverse Scattering for Single Photons in Quantum Optics'] Let $k_\rho$ be the threshold from Lemma \ref{lem_LAP} with $l=[n/2]+1$ and $\delta=3/4$. Let $k>k_\rho$ and let $\alpha,\theta\in\mathbb S^{n-1}$ satisfy
$\theta\neq\alpha$. Then $\mathcal I_\rho(\alpha,k,\theta,\cdot)$ determines the scattering amplitude $A_k(\theta,\alpha)$.
More precisely,
\begin{equation}
    A_k(\theta,\alpha)
    =
    \lim_{R\to\infty}
    \frac{1}{R}
    \int_R^{2R}
    \mathcal I_\rho(\alpha,k,\theta,r)
    e^{-ikr(1-\alpha\cdot\theta)}\,dr .
\end{equation}

