[Definition def-u-m of arXiv:2604.24914, 'SPDEs with time-independent\\ L\'evy colored noise'] {\rm The process $\{u(t,x);t\geq 0,x\in \mathbb{R}^d\}$ with $\mathbb{E}|u(t,x)|^2<\infty$ for all $(t,x) \in \mathbb{R}_{+} \times \mathbb{R}^d$ and the Poisson-chaos expansion:
\begin{equation}

u(t,x)=1+\sum_{n\geq 1}I_n\big(f_n^{*}(\cdot,x;t)\big),
\end{equation}
is the {\bf (Skorohod) solution} of equation (equation mult-eq of the paper), provided that $f_n^{*}(\cdot,x;t)\in \mathcal{H}^{\otimes n}$ for any $(t,x)\in \mathbb{R}_{+}\times \mathbb{R}^d$ and $n\geq 1$, and the series converges in $L^2(\Omega)$.
}

[Lemma lem:GaussianEigenvalues2 of arXiv:2410.23915, 'Asymptotic Bounds and Online Algorithms for Average-Case Matrix Discrepancy'] Let $X,Y$ be two $m \times m$ GOE matrices with correlation $\rho \in (-1,1)$. The joint probability density function of their ordered eigenvalues $\lambda_1(X) \leq \ldots \leq \lambda_m(X)$ and $\mu_1(X) \leq \ldots \leq \mu_m(X)$ is bounded above by
        \begin{equation}

            (\lambda,\mu) \mapsto C_m^2 (1 - \rho^2)^{-m(m+1)/4} \exp{-\frac{\left\lVert\ifblank{\lambda}{\:\cdot\:}{\lambda}\right\rVert_2^2 - 2\rho\inp{\lambda}{\mu} + \left\lVert\ifblank{\mu}{\:\cdot\:}{\mu}\right\rVert_2^2}{4(1 - \rho^2)}} \Delta(\lambda)\Delta(\mu)
        \end{equation}
        on $\mathbb{R}^m_\geq \times \mathbb{R}^m_\geq$, where the constant $C_m$ is defined as in (equation eq:NormalizationConstant2 of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

