body:
[Lem lem-green-conv of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] Let $\mathcal A\subset\mathcal V\mathcal G$ be finite and non-empty. Let $\{\mathcal G_n\}_{n\geq 1}$ be an increasing family of connected subgraphs of $\mathcal G$ whose union is all of $\mathcal G$ such that $\mathcal A\subset\mathcal V\mathcal G_n$ for every $n\in\mathbbm N$. 
For $n\in\mathbbm N$, let $G_{\mathcal A}^n$ be the Green's function for random walk on $\mathcal G_n$ killed when it first hits $\mathcal A$. 
Then for each $x,y\in\mathcal V\mathcal G$, 
\begin{equation}  
\lim_{n\to\infty} \mathcal G_{\mathcal A}^n(x,y) = \mathcal G_{\mathcal A}(x,y) .
\end{equation}

