[Definition 1 of arXiv:2608.12070, 'Central limit theorems for a heavy-tailed subcritical Galton-Watson process with state-dep'] If there exists a function $L$ slowly varying at infinity such that the random variable $Z$ satisfies
\begin{align}
\mathbb{P}(|Z|>x)\sim  x^{-\alpha}L(x), \quad x\rightarrow \infty,

\end{align}
then $Z$ is said to have a regularly varying tail with index $\alpha$.

