body:
[Theorem thm1 of arXiv:2411.09716, 'Stable Tables'] The probability $f(n)$ that a given person is unmatched at a table with $n$ people is
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{1}{9} + \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^n\left(\frac{2n}{3} - \frac{8}{9} + \frac{2}{n}\right)
    \end{equation}
    when $n$ is odd, and
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{1}{9} - \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^n\left(\frac{2n}{3} - \frac{8}{9}\right)
    \end{equation}
    when $n$ is even. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem: link between Pi and K of arXiv:2509.04349, 'Precise asymptotics for the norm of large random rectangular Toeplitz matrices'] The constant $K_{1,n/p}$ satisfies
    \begin{equation}
K_{1,n/p}=\frac{\sup_{\mathbf{c}_1,\mathbf{c}_2\in\ell^2(\mathbb{C}):\|\mathbf{c}_1\|=\|\mathbf{c}_2\|=1}\|\Pi_{p/N}\mathbf{c}_1\odot \Pi_{n/N}\mathbf{c}_2\|}{\sqrt{p/N}},
\end{equation}
where $\odot$ denotes the entrywise multiplication of vectors from $\ell^2(\mathbb{C})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

