[Proposition prop-kinetic of arXiv:2507.09922, 'A scaling limit for Vlasov equations with electrostatic fluctuations'] Fix $\delta>0$. For any $t>0$, it holds
  \begin{equation}
  \mathcal K(f^\delta_t) + \mathcal V_\delta (f^\delta_t)= \mathcal K(f^\delta_0) + \mathcal V_\delta(f^\delta_0) + 6\kappa t \|f^\delta_0\|_{L^1_{x,v}} +M_t,
  \end{equation}
where $M_t$ is a square integrable martingale with quadratic variation
  $$[M]_t \le 24\kappa \|f^\delta_0 \|_{L^1_{x,v}} \int_0^t\mathcal K(f^\delta_s)\, ds. $$

