[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2608.12070, 'Central limit theorems for a heavy-tailed subcritical Galton-Watson process with state-dep'] Suppose the process $\mathbf{X}=\{X_n:n\geq0\}$ is defined by \eqref{111} and satisfies {\bf (B)}. Then as $n\to \infty$,  
\begin{align*}
\frac{S_n-\beta K_n/(1-m)}{a_n}\stackrel{d}{\rightarrow} \pi_0^{-1/\alpha}\zeta_\alpha,
\end{align*}
  where  $\{a_n\}$ is an integer-valued sequence satisfying $na_n^{-\alpha}l_2(a_n)\to\beta^{-1}(1-m)^{1+\alpha}$, and $\zeta_\alpha$ is an $\alpha$-stable random variable with characteristic function$$\psi(t)=\exp\left(- |t| ^\alpha\Gamma(1-\alpha)\cos\frac{\pi\alpha}{2} (1+\mathrm{i}\mathrm{sgn}(t)\tan\frac{\pi\alpha}{2}) \right),\quad t\in\mathbb{R}.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 1 (Main result of  stability) of arXiv:2604.15191, 'Quantitative Stability of Many-Marginal Schr\"odinger Bridge'] Let $(\rho_t^\mu)_{t\in[0, 1]}$ and $(\rho_t^\nu)_{t\in[0, 1]}$ be two density evolution curves over $\mb T^d$. 
Given time points $0 = t_0 < t_1 < \cdots < t_m = 1$, take $\bm\mu^m = (\rho^\mu_{t_0}, \cdots, \rho_{t_m}^\mu)$ and $\bm\nu^m = (\rho_{t_0}^\nu, \cdots, \rho_{t_m}^\nu)$ as marginal constraints.

Suppose that there exists $L_\rho\in(0, 1)$, such that
\begin{align*}
L_\rho \leq \rho_t^\mu(x), \rho_{t_j}^\nu(x) \leq L_\rho^{-1} \quad \hbox{uniformly for all $t\in[0, 1]$, $j\in\{0, 1, \cdots, m\}$, and $x\in\mb T^d$.}
\end{align*}

Let $R^{\bm\nu^m}$ and $R^{\bm\mu^m}$ be the multi-marginal Schr\"odinger bridges \eqref{eqn:SB-multi} connecting $\bm \nu^m$ and $\bm\mu^m$, respectively.
Under Assumption~\ref{assump: density_expansion} on $(\rho_t^\mu)_{t\in[0, 1]}$, 

we have {\yh [We also need to explain the dependence of $\lesssim$..]}
\begin{align}
\KL(R^{\bm\nu^m}\,\|\,R^{\bm\mu^m}) 
\lesssim \big[\KL(\rho_0^\nu\,\|\,\rho_0^\mu) + \W_1(\rho_0^\nu, \rho_0^\mu)^{\frac{1}{3}}\big] + \sum_{j=1}^m\varepsilon_j\W_1(\rho_{t_j}^\nu, \rho_{t_j}^\mu)^{\frac{1}{3}} + \int_0^1\FI(\bar\rho_t^\nu\,\|\,\bar \rho_t^\mu)\,\dd t +
o_m(1),

\end{align}
\rytodo{where the big-O notation omits a constant depending only on xxx},
both $(\bar\rho_t^\mu)_{t\in[0, 1]}$and  $(\bar\rho_t^\nu)_{t\in[0, 1]}$ are piecewise $\W_2$-geodesics determined by the marginals at the time points $t_j$'s with $j=0, 1, .., m$,  and
\begin{align*}
\FI(\bar\rho_t^\nu\,\|\,\bar\rho_t^\mu) \coloneqq \int_{\mb T^d}\bigg\|\nabla\log\frac{\bar\rho_t^\nu}{\bar\rho_t^\mu}\bigg\|^2\,\dd\bar\rho_t^\nu
\end{align*}
is the relative Fisher information between $\bar\rho_t^\nu$ and $\bar\rho_t^\mu$.
\myqed (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

