body:
[Corollary m-cor of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] Under the hypotheses of Theorem (mt1 of the paper), there exists a finite
constant ${\mathfrak c}_0 = {\mathfrak c}_0({\boldsymbol u}^N)$, depending only
on ${\boldsymbol u}^N$ and uniformly bounded in $N$, such that
\begin{equation*}
H_N(f^N_t) \;\leq\; 
(N/\ell_N)^d\, e^{{\mathfrak c}_0 \, K^2_N \, t}
\end{equation*}
for all $t\ge 0$, $N\ge 1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

