[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2604.25769, 'The conformal dimension of the Brownian tree is one'] For each $\eta > 0$, there exists a metric $D_\sigma$ on $X$ and a constant $C > 0$ such that the identity mapping $\mathrm{id} \colon (X, D) \to (X, D_\sigma)$ is quasisymmetric and
    \begin{equation*}
        \diam(B_{\alpha^n}(x; D); D_\sigma) \le C \prod_{j = 1}^n \left(\eta + 2\sup\{\sigma(y, j) : y \in X \text{ with } D(x, y) \le 26\alpha^j\}\right), \quad \forall (x, n) \in V. 
    \end{equation*}

