[Proposition 8 (Product--sum formula) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] For any $n, m\geqs0$, one has 
\begin{equation}

 H_n(x) H_m(x) = \sum_{p=0}^{n\wedge m} 
 p! \binom{n}{p} \binom{m}{p} H_{n+m-2p}(x)\;,
\end{equation} 
where $n\wedge m$ denotes the minimum of $n$ and $m$.

