body:
[Thm persistence of arXiv:2411.05235, 'A comparative study of three mathematical approaches applied to the reversal of AMR'] If \( \mathcal{K}_{0}^{s} > 1 \) 
    , then there exists \( \xi_{s} \in (0, N) \) such that for any \( R_0 \in (0, N) \), the following holds:
\begin{equation}
   \limsup_{t \to \infty} R(\cdot, t; R_0) \geq \xi_{s}, \quad \mathbb{P}-\text{a.s.}
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
   \liminf_{t \to \infty} R(\cdot, t; R_0) \leq \xi_{s}, \quad \mathbb{P}-\text{a.s.}
\end{equation}
where \( \xi_{s} \) is given by
\[
\xi_{s} = \frac{\sigma^{2}N - \beta - \sqrt{\beta^2 - 2\sigma^2(\gamma + \mu)}}{\sigma^2 +\epsilon\beta +\epsilon \sqrt{\beta^2 - 2\sigma^2(\gamma + \mu)}}.
\]
In other words, the solution process \( R(\cdot,\cdot\ ; R_0) \) visits the level \( \xi_{s} \) infinitely often for any \( R_0 \in (0, N) \).

[Theorem 13 of arXiv:2608.06011, 'Strong averaging principle for multiscale time-inhomogeneous SDEs with multiplicative $\al'] Suppose that Assumptions \ref{cond} and \ref{con:periodic} hold. Then, the SDE \eqref{frozen SDE} admits a unique continuous periodic measure $\rho_t^{x}$ with period $\tau_2$, which satisfies 
    \begin{equation}
        \cw_1(P^x(s-n\tau_2,y,t,\cdot),\rho_t^x)\leq C(1+|x|+|y|)\re^{-(\lambda-q)n\tau_2}.
    \end{equation}
    Furthermore, for all $p\in[1,\alpha)$, there exists $C_{\kappa,p}>0$ such that 
    \begin{equation}
        \int_{\br^m}|w|^p\rho_t^{x}(\d w)\leq C_{\kappa,p}(1+|x|^p).
    \end{equation}

