[Theorem MLSI DOWN UP MC of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] Let $\ensuremath{\mathcal B}$ be a fixed partition of $[L]$. Suppose that \(\Lambda\) is a nonnegative definite $L\times L$ matrix with largest eigenvalue \(\lambda(\Lambda) < 1/2\). Then 
for all values of the vector $\ensuremath{\mathcal M}$, for all $w\in{\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} ^L$,
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{E}^{\rm du}_\ensuremath{\mathcal B}(F, \log F)\ge (1 - 2\lambda(\Lambda))^2\, \mathrm{Ent}_{\nu_{L,\ensuremath{\mathcal M}}} (F) \,,
\end{equation}
for every \(F : \Omega_{L,\ensuremath{\mathcal M}} \to {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} _+\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

