[Corollary 10 of arXiv:2608.29143, 'Least Variability in a Polynomial-Square Class\\ of Rational Kernels'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{rig:thm:rigidity}, let
\[
    n=
    \begin{cases}
        m+1,&\deg a_*=m-1,\\
        m+2,&\deg a_*=m.
    \end{cases}
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
    R_*a_*=c\Lag_n
\end{equation}
for some \(c\neq0\), and the roots \(x,y\) of \(R_*\) are zeros of \(\Lag_n\). Consequently,
\begin{equation}
    a_*(t)
    =c\frac{\Lag_n(t)}{(t-x)(t-y)}.
\end{equation}

[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Assume that $X=(X_1,\ldots,X_N)$ is a diffusion process defined in \eqref{defn:x} such that $X(0)\in \C$. If the continuity assumption \ref{ass:cont}, \ref{ass:sigma} together with \ref{ass:k:positive} hold, then for every $\alpha\in R_+$
            \begin{equation}

        \int_0^t \frac{k_\alpha(s,X(s))}{\left<X(s),\alpha\right>}ds<\infty\/,\quad 
    \end{equation}
    for every $t<\life{X}$.

