[Definition def_good of arXiv:2608.09105, 'Longest convex chains with i.i.d.\ points'] Given $\eta>0$ and $\delta>0$, we say the sample set $\mathcal{S}_n$ is \textit{$(\eta,\delta)$-good} if
\eeq{ 
\#\big(\mathcal{S}_n\cap([1-\eta,1]\times[0,1])\big)\leqslant\delta n \qquad \text{and} \qquad
\#\big(\mathcal{S}_n\cap([0,1]\times[0,\eta])\big)\leqslant\delta n.
}
Otherwise we say $\mathcal{S}_n$ is \textit{$(\eta,\delta)$-bad}.
\hfill\ensuremath{\square}

[Corollary 62 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Suppose that Assumptions~\ref{Assumptions_Theta} and \ref{Assumptions_basic}
hold. Then for any $\delta>0$, there exists a constant $C >0$ depending only on $\delta$ and the constants in the assumptions, such that
for any $t > 0$ and any $z$ at distance greater than $\delta$ from $\amsmathbb{A}$ we have
\begin{equation}

\amsmathbb{P}_{\N}\Bigg[\bigg|\frac{\Delta G_h(z)}{\N}\bigg| \geq t\Bigg] \leq \exp\bigg(C \N\log \N -
\frac{t^2\N^2}{C}\bigg).
\end{equation}
In addition for any $\eps>0$, any positive integer $n$, any $h_1,\ldots,h_n \in [H]$ and $z_1,\ldots,z_n \in\amsmathbb C$ such that $\min_{i} \textnormal{dist}(z_i,\amsmathbb{A}) \geq \delta$, we have
 \begin{equation}
  \E\Bigg[\bigg|
\prod_{i=1}^n \Delta G_{h_i}(z_i)\bigg|\Bigg] \leq \N^{n(\frac{1}{2}+\eps)} + n \bigg(\frac{\N}{\delta}\bigg)^n \exp\bigg(C \N\log \N -
\frac{\N^{1+2\eps}}{C}\bigg).
 \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

