[Lemma def:irreducibility22 of arXiv:2510.00748, '\bf On irreducible central limit theorems'] Let the assumptions and conventions of the present section hold. Then, the sequence $\{Z_n\}$ is reducible in the sense of Definition (def:irreducibility of the paper) (see also Remark (r:reducible of the paper)-{\rm (redCLTconda of the paper),(redCLTcondb of the paper),(redCLTcondc of the paper)}) if and only if there exist partitions $\{B_1,\ldots,B_{m_n}\} = \{B^{(n)}_1,\ldots,B^{(n)}_{m_n}\}$ of the vertex sets $V_n$, such that, as $n \to \infty$,
    \begin{enumerate}[label={\rm (\roman*')}]
    \item  $m_n\to \infty$;
    \item  $\sum_{i=1}^{m_n} E(B_i,B_i) \sim |\mathcal{E}_n|$;
    \item  $\max_{i=1,...,m_n} E(B_i,B_i) = o\big(|\mathcal{E}_n|\big)$.  
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

