body:
[Proposition 16 (Eigenvalue master equation — Wishart case) of arXiv:2511.12623, 'The eigenvector bead process'] Fix integers $N, T \ge 1$, and let $\{\lambda_i\}_{i=1}^{N}$ denote the (positive) eigenvalues of $X_{N}^{\!\top} X_{N}$.
Consider the rank-one extension
\[
X_{N+1} \;=\; \big( X_N \;\; g \big),
\qquad g \in \mathbb{R}^{T},
\]
that is, $X_{N+1}$ is obtained by appending the column vector $g$ to $X_N$.
Then the eigenvalues $z$ of $X_{N+1}^{\!\top} X_{N+1}$ are the zeros of the \emph{secular equation}
\begin{equation}
F_N(z)
\;=\;
1
+ \sum_{i=1}^{N}
\frac{|\langle v_i, g \rangle|^2}{\lambda_i - z}
- \frac{\Gamma}{z}
\;=\;0,
\end{equation}
where ${v_i}$ are the eigenvectors associated with the nonzero eigenvalues of $X_N X_N^{\top}$, and
\(
\Gamma
:= \sum_{j=1}^{T-N} |\langle w_j, g \rangle|^2,
\)
with $\{w_j\}$ forming an orthonormal basis of the null space of $X_{N} X_{N}^{\!\top}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:mvsde-coming-down of arXiv:2411.01364, 'Global Dynamics of Granular Media Equations via Stochastic Order'] Suppose Assumption (asp:potential of the paper) holds.
If $\xi\in L^2(\Omega,\mathcal F_0,\mathbf P)$, then $X_t^{\xi}\in L^p(\Omega,\mathcal F_t,\mathbf P)$ for all $p\geq2$, $t>0$.
Moreover, for any $p\geq2$, there exists a constant $C(p)\geq1$ such that, for all $t\geq1$,
\begin{equation*}
\big(\mathbf E\big[|X_t^{\xi}|^p\big]\big)^{1/p}\leq\mathrm e^{-(t-1)}\big(\mathbf E[|\xi|^2]\big)^{1/2}+C(p).
\end{equation*}

