[Corollary 14 of arXiv:2511.02725, 'Mixing of general biased adjacent transposition chains'] Suppose $\vec{p}$ is $\eps$-positively biased and $\vec{\ell} \in \mathcal L_n$. For $k \ge 1$, let 
    \begin{align*}
       X = \min\{s: \sigma(s) \le k\} \,.
    \end{align*}
    Then, the law of $X$ under $\mu (\cdot \mid \vell\loc)$ is stochastically below a geometric random variable with success probability $1- (1+\eps)^{-k}$.

