[Definition of arXiv:2606.19313, 'Stability of Khintchine-type inequalities via log-monotonicity'] Let $q\geq 2$ be an integer. For $a\in\mathbb{R}^n$ satisfying $\sum_ka_k^2=1$, define
\begin{align*}
0\leq \Delta_q(a)=\begin{cases} 1& n<q,\\
1-q!\binom{n}{q}\Big( \frac{1-\sum_ka_k^4}{n(n-1)}\Big)^{\frac{q}{2}}& n\geq q.
\end{cases}
\end{align*}

[Lemma lem:uniqueness of arXiv:2608.18293, 'Critical tensor covariance at the Marchenko--Pastur threshold'] Let $\nu$ be any probability measure on $[0,\infty)$, $c>0$, and $z\in\mathbb{C}_+$. The equation
\begin{equation}
  \frac1m+z
  =\int_0^\infty\frac{r}{1+crm}\,\nu(\,\mathrm{d} r)

\end{equation}
has at most one solution $m\in\mathbb{C}_+$.

