[Lem 13 of arXiv:2608.16144, 'Central limit theorem in R\'enyi divergence for lattice random variables'] For any polynomial $f(x)$ of degree at most $d\geq 0$, we have
\begin{equation*} 
\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}f(x_{n,k})q_{n,k}=\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x) \varphi(x)~dx+O(e^{-\pi^2n/h}).
\end{equation*}

