[Theorem BerryEsseen of arXiv:2411.14876, 'Limit theorems for stochastic exponentials of matrix-valued L\'evy processes \\'] Let $L$ be a L\'evy process in $\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}$ fulfilling (equation eq-nonsingular of the paper) and let $X$ be the corresponding stochastic exponential.
	Assume that $G_X$ satisfies  (i-p) and $\mathds{E} \big[ \sup_{0 \le s \le 1} (\log M(X_s))^4 \big]<\infty$. Then there is a constant $C>0$ such that for all $n \ge 1$, $y \in \R^d$ with $\|y \|=1$ and $z \in \R$,
\begin{equation}
	\bigg| \mathds{P} \bigg(\frac{\log \|Y_t^y \|-t\lambda}{\sigma \sqrt{t}} \le z\bigg) -  \Phi(z)  \bigg| ~\le~\frac{C}{\sqrt{t}}. 
\end{equation}
Under the additional assumption that $\mathds{E} \big[ M(X_1)^\delta\big]<\infty$ for some $\delta>0$,  there exist $C>0$ and $\gamma>0$ such that for all $n \ge 1$, $y \in \R^d$ with $\|y \|=1$, $z \in \R$ and $\varphi \in \mathcal{B}_\gamma$,
	\begin{equation}
		\bigg| \mathds{E} \bigg[ \varphi(Z_t^{\hat{y}}) \mathds{1}\bigg\{\frac{\log \|Y_t^y \|-t\lambda}{\sigma \sqrt{t}} \le z\bigg\}\bigg] - \pi(\varphi) \Phi(z)  \bigg| ~\le~\frac{C}{\sqrt{t}} \|\varphi \|_\gamma .
	\end{equation}

