body:
[Corollary semigroup of arXiv:2606.28575, 'Global smooth solutions by high mode Lie-Transport noise for Logarithmically Hyperdissipat'] $A:X_1\subseteq X_0\rightarrow X_0$ generates an analytic semigroup of negative type on $X_0$ which we denote by $e^{At}$. Moreover, $-A$ admits a bounded $H^{\infty}$ calculus with angle zero. Finally, for $\theta\in (0,1),$ and  $p\in [1,+\infty]$, setting 
\begin{align*}
    D_A(\theta,p)=\Big\{x\in X_0:t\rightarrow v_t=\norm{t^{1-\theta-\frac{1}{p}}A e^{At}x}_{X_0}\in L^p(0,1)\Big\}
\end{align*}
endowed with the norm $\left\|x\right\|_{D_A(\alpha,p)}=\left\|x\right\|_{X_0}+\left\|v\right\|_{L^p(0,1)}$,
it holds
\begin{align}
    [X_0,X_1]_{\theta}&=D((-A)^{\theta})= H^{2(\theta-1)}_g,\\

    \left(X_0,X_1\right)_{\theta,p}&=D_A(\theta,p)=B^{2(\theta-1)}_{g,2,p},\\

    D_A(\theta,1)&\hookrightarrow D((-A)^{\theta})\hookrightarrow D_A(\theta,\infty).
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 3 (Eyring--Kramers law) of arXiv:2607.20882, 'An Eyring--Kramers Law for the Hypoelliptic Third-Order\\ Langevin Diffusion'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:double-well} and~\ref{ass:growth-lyapunov}, as
$\eps\downarrow0$,
\begin{equation}

\E_{(m,0,0)}[\tau_{S_\eps}]
=
[1+o_\eps(1)]
\frac{2\pi}{\mu_\sigma}
\sqrt{\frac{-\det H_\sigma}{\det H_m}}
\exp\!\left(\frac{U(\sigma)-U(m)}{\eps}\right),
\end{equation}
where $\mu_\sigma>0$ is the unique positive root of the cubic equation \eqref{eq:cubic}.

