body:
[Prop ilocal of arXiv:2601.20502, 'Optimal matching under size priority'] Under condition~(eq:uniquefixedpoint of the paper), for any edge weight distribution, the macroscopic marginal $i$ in $\left(\mathbb{T},o,w,(i,Z)(u,v)_{(u,v)\in \overset{\rightarrow}{\mathbb{T}}}\right)$ from Proposition~(prop:Zconstruction of the paper) is measurable in the weightless tree $(\mathbb{T},o)$.  In addition, $(\mathbb{T},o)$-\emph{a.e.}, there exists a unique family $(i(u,v))_{(u,v)\in\overset{\rightarrow}{E}(\mathbb{T})}$ verifying
    \begin{equation}
        \forall (u,v) \in \overset{\rightarrow}{E}(\mathbb{T}) , \, i(u,v)=\max\left(0,\max_{\substack{u' \sim v \\ u'\neq u }} (1-i(v,u')) \right).
    \end{equation}

