body:
[Lemma quadraticterm of arXiv:2608.23765, '\texorpdfstring{Tight Majorizations and Convergence Rates\\ of Nuclear Norm Minimization I'] Assume that
	\begin{equation*}
		 \mathcal{A} \left(\mathbf{X}_\star \right) = \mathcal{A} \left(\mathbf{X} \right)
	\end{equation*}
	and that the measurement operator $\mathcal{A}: \mathbb{R}^{d_1 \times d_2} \longrightarrow \R^m $ 
	satisfies the NSP of order $r$ of (def:NSP:statement of the paper) for some constant $0<\eta_r<1$, and the NSP of order $1$ with $0 < \eta_1 < 1$. 
	Let $ \W{\mathbf{X}}{\varepsilon}(\cdot)$ be defined as in (def:optimalweightoperator of the paper). Then
	\begin{equation}
	\innerproduct{\mathbf{X}_\star - \mathbf{X} , \W{\mathbf{X}}{\varepsilon} (\mathbf{X}_\star - \mathbf{X}) }  \leq  \frac{ \eta_1 \nucnorm{ \mathbf{X}_\star - \mathbf{X} }^2  }{\varepsilon},
	\end{equation}	
	if the weight operator core matrix $\mathbf{H}_{\boldsymbol{\sigma}, \varepsilon}$ of $\W{\mathbf{X}}{\varepsilon}(\cdot)$ corresponds to harmonic mean (eq:harmonic:mean of the paper), one-sided weights (eq:leftsided:mean,eq:rightsided:mean of the paper), or power mean weights (eq:power:mean:core:matrix of the paper) with $q \in [-\infty, 1]$, and
	\begin{equation}
		\innerproduct{\mathbf{X}_\star - \mathbf{X} , \W{\mathbf{X}}{\varepsilon} (\mathbf{X}_\star - \mathbf{X}) }  \leq \frac{ c_q \eta_1 \nucnorm{ \mathbf{X}_\star - \mathbf{X} }^2  }{\varepsilon} \leq  \frac{ 3 \eta_1 \nucnorm{ \mathbf{X}_\star - \mathbf{X} }^2  }{\varepsilon},
		\end{equation}	
	if $\mathbf{H}_{\boldsymbol{\sigma}, \varepsilon}$ corresponds to power mean weights (eq:power:mean:core:matrix of the paper) with $q \in (1,\infty]$, where $c_q$ is the constant (eq:c_q:def of the paper).

