body:
[Theorem eq:limitingF_SSK of arXiv:2510.26960, 'Free energy fluctuations in SK and related spin glass models: \\ A literature survey'] When no external field is present ($h=0$), the free energy of SSK exhibits the following convergence in distribution as $N\to\infty$.
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item In the high temperature regime, $\beta<1$,
 \begin{equation} 
N(F_N(\beta)-F(\beta))\to\mathcal{N}(-\frac12 \sigma^2,\sigma^2)
 \end{equation} 
where
$\sigma^2=-\frac12\log(1-\beta^2)$.  

\item In the low temperature regime, $\beta>1$,
 \begin{equation} 
\frac{2N^{2/3}}{\beta-1}(F_N(\beta)-F(\beta))\to TW_1.
 \end{equation} 
\end{enumerate} 
The limiting free energy $F(\beta)$ in this setting is given by the formula
 \begin{equation} 
F(\beta)=\begin{cases}
\frac14\beta^2& \text{for }\beta\leq1,\\
\beta-\frac12\log\beta-\frac34 & \text{for }\beta\geq1.
\end{cases}
 \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Cor 7. cor: GW tree satisfies the sub-aging assumption of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] Define a probability measure $\tilde{p} = (\tilde{p}_{k})_{k \geq 1}$ on $\mathbb{N}$ 
  by setting $\tilde{p}_{k} \coloneqq p_{k-1}$.
  Then, it holds that 
  \begin{equation}
    (T_{n}^{GW}, n^{-1/2}d_{T_{n}^{GW}}, \rho_{T_{n}^{GW}}, n^{-1} \dot{\mu}^{\#}_{T_{n}^{GW}})
    \xrightarrow{\mathrm{d}}
    (T_{2e}, d_{2e}, \rho_{2e}, \mu_{2e} \otimes \tilde{p})
  \end{equation}
  in the space $\mathfrak{M}_{c}(\markedfinMeasFunct{\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}})$.

