    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel.  

    Then

    \begin{multline}
        \mathbf{P}_{\beta}
        \left(
            o 
            \leftrightarrow 
            B(r)^c, 
            \# K
            \leq 
            k(r)
        \right) 
        \\
        \leq 
        \sum_{\substack{
            b \in \mathbf{N}
            \\
            \mathbf{m} \in \mathcal{M}(b)
            \\
            \mathbf{r} \in \mathcal{R}(b,\mathbf{m},r)
            \\
            \mathbf{A} \in \mathcal{A}(b,\mathbf{m})
        }}
        \sum_{\substack{
            \ell \in \mathbf{N}
            \\
            \mathbf{B} \in \mathcal{A}'(\ell,\mathbf{A})
