[Lemma 54 of arXiv:2608.03575, '2608.03575'] The sequence \((\log R_n)_{n\geq1}\) is stationary and integrable.
Consequently, there exists a finite, shift-invariant random variable
\(\lambda\) such that
\begin{equation}
    \lim_{n\to\infty}
    \frac{-\log\widehat r(X_n)}{n}
    =
    \lambda
\end{equation}
almost surely. If the marked random rooted ADT
\((G,\rho,\Theta)\) is ergodic, then \(\lambda\) is almost surely
constant.

