[Lemma lem_usc of arXiv:2608.09105, 'Longest convex chains with i.i.d.\ points'] Let $\mu_n, \mu \in \mathcal{M}$.
Fix $t\in[0,1)$.
If $\mu_n\big|_{[0,t]}$ converges weakly to $\mu\big|_{[0,t]}$ as $n\to\infty$, then for any continuous function $w\colon[0,t] \to [0, \infty)$, we have
\eeq{ 
\limsup_{n\to\infty}\int_0^{t} w(x)\cdot D_{\mu_n}(x)^{1/3}\ \mathrm{d} x  \leqslant  \int_0^{t} w(x)\cdot D_\mu(x)^{1/3}\ \mathrm{d} x.
}

