[Definition def:bg-gmp of arXiv:2607.05226, 'The Exact Worst-Case Tail Probability under Bounded Kurtosis'] Given a Borel event $S\subseteq\mathbb{R}$ and finitely many prescribed moments (values or
bounds), the \emph{generalized moment problem} is the linear program over probability
measures that extremizes $\mu(S)$ subject to the moment constraints. The quantity
$V_{1}(t,\kappa)$ of (sec:prelim of the paper) is the instance
\begin{equation}
\sup_{\mu}\;\;\mu(S)
\qquad\text{s.t.}\quad
\textstyle\int\!d\mu=1,\;\;
\int\!x\,d\mu=0,\;\;
\int\!x^2\,d\mu=1,\;\;
\int\!x^4\,d\mu\le\kappa,
\end{equation}
with $S=[t,\infty)$.

[Lemma l19b of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] There exists a finite constant ${\mathfrak c}({\boldsymbol u}^N)$ such that 
\begin{equation*}
\begin{aligned}
& {\mathbb E}_{\nu^N} \Big[\,
\Big|\;
\int_0^t {\mathcal F}^{(2)}_\ell (s,\eta^N(s)) \, ds \, \Big|
\,-\, \int_0^t  \Psi  (s,\eta^N(s)) \, ds
\,\Big]
\\
&\quad  \;\le\; \frac{\log 2}{K} \;+\; 
{\mathfrak c}({\boldsymbol u}^N) \, K\, (N/\ell)^{d} \, t
\end{aligned}
\end{equation*}
for all $t>0$ and  $N\ge 1$.

