[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2609.01296, 'Asymptotic safety regions for Gabor frames generated by Hermite functions'] Let $ r, M > 0$ and $\Phi:[M,+\infty)$ be differentiable and convex.  If
    \begin{equation}
        \gamma:=\frac{r}{M} -\Phi'(M)<0,
    \end{equation}
    then for every $T \ge M$, the inequality
    \begin{equation}
        \sum\limits_{l = 0}^{\infty} (T+l)^r e^{-\Phi(T+l)} \leq \frac{M^r e^{-\Phi( M)}}{1-e^{\gamma}}
    \end{equation}
    holds.

