[Proposition Prop: upper bound for X epsilon of arXiv:2606.19207, 'Extrema of cooling branching Brownian motion and related Gaussian fields'] Fix $\alpha\in(0,1/2]$. For $\varepsilon\in(0,1)$, set $T:=\log(1/\varepsilon)$ and let $X_\varepsilon^\alpha$ be the Gaussian field defined in (equation eqModel: X epsilon alpha white noise integral of the paper). There exist constants $C,c>0$ and $T_*,\lambda_*>0$ such that
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{P}\Bigl(
		\sup_{x\in[0,1)^d}X_\varepsilon^\alpha(x)
		\geq A_\alpha(T)+\lambda
		\Bigr)
		\leq Ce^{-c\lambda}
	\end{equation}
	for every $T\geq T_*$ and $\lambda\geq\lambda_*$, where $A_\alpha(T)$ is given by (equation eqIntroduction: A(t) of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem Prop4:13 of arXiv:2412.06086, 'Zeros of conditional Gaussian analytic functions, random sub-unitary matrices and q-series'] Consider the rescaled point process $\mathcal{V}_a$ defined by the transformation
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{Q}_a=1- \frac{\log t - \log\log t + \mathcal{V}_a }{t}\,, \quad t=|a|^2,
\end{align*}
where $\mathcal{Q}_a$ is the set  of absolute squares of the zeros of $\varphi_a(z)=a+\sum_{k\ge 1} c_k z^k$. The rescaled process $\mathcal{V}_a$  converges in distribution, as   $a\to\infty$, to Poisson point process on $\mathbb{R}$ with intensity $\lambda (v)= e^{-v}$.

