[Prop maximum_principle of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Suppose that $q, q_+, q_-$ are a solution, supersolution, and subsolution respectively to the critical gauge equation $\mathcal{C}_n(\cdot)= 1$ on a region $U\subset B\cap \varepsilon\Lambda$. Then 
	\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
		\item the minimum value of $q/q_-$ over $U$ is realized on $\partial U$. 
		\item the maximum value of $q/q_+$ over $U$ is realized on $\partial U$;
	\end{enumerate}

