[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2512.02922, 'Asymptotics for additive functionals of particle systems via Stein's method'] We have  that  \begin{align}
d_{W}(\rho_r,\gamma)
  \leq 	\frac{\sqrt{2}}{\sigma_r^3}\int_{\R^d}\E\left[\left|\int_0^r\langle\mu^x_s,\psi\rangle ds\right|^3\right] \nu(dx).
\end{align}
Moreover, under the condition $\psi\geq 0$,  the following third moment theorem holds
\begin{align}
d_{W}(\rho_r,\gamma)
  \leq 	\sqrt{2}m_{3}[\rho_r].
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition XY height function on a percolation configuration of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Given an integer $L \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, an integer $n\geq 2$, a parameter $\lambda > 0$, two inverse temperatures $\beta_1 , \beta_2 \geq 0$ and a percolation configuration $r \in \{0,1\}^{\Lambda_L},$ we define
  \begin{equation*}
     \mu_{L , n ,\beta_1, \beta_2 , \lambda, r}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}} - \mathrm{XY}} (\left\{ \varphi \right\}) := \frac{1}{Z_{\Lambda_L,J, r}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}} }  I_{\left(\varphi(0)\right)} \left( \lambda \right)\prod_{x \sim y}  \left[ I_{\left(\varphi(x) - \varphi(y)\right)} \left( r_x \beta_1 \right) I_{\left(\varphi(x) - \varphi(y)\right)} \left( r_y \beta_1 \right) I_{\left(\varphi(x) - \varphi(y)\right)} \left(  n \beta_2 \right)^{n-2} \right].
 \end{equation*}
 We denote the variance associated with this measure by $\mathrm{Var}_{L , n ,\beta_1, \beta_2 , \lambda, r}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}} - \mathrm{XY}}$.

[Lemma lem:asep-dressing of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The gauged kernel (equation eq:asep-gauged-kernel of the paper) satisfies
