[Theorem thm:trel_svgap of arXiv:2607.10801, 'Relaxation times of non-reversible\\ Markov processes'] It holds
    \begin{equation*}
        \frac{2(1-e^{-1})}{\sing(\mathcal{L})}\ \leq \ \overline t_\mathrm{rel}(P)\ \leq \ \frac{2e}{\sing(\mathcal{L})} \quad\text{ and }\quad
        \frac{1-e^{-1}}{\sing(\mathcal{L})}\ \leq \ t_\mathrm{rel}(P)\,.
    \end{equation*}
    Moreover,
    \begin{equation}
        \| \overline P_tf\|\ \le\ \frac{2}{t\cdot \sing(\mathcal{L})}\| f\|\quad\text{ for all }f\in L^2_0(\mu )\text{ and }t>0\,.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary of arXiv:2411.08846, 'On the Number of Crossings and Bouncings\\ of a Diffusion at a Sticky Threshold'] We consider the setting of Theorem~(thm_main_R of the paper) and $\mathcal H_t $ be the event $\{\tau^{X}_0<t\} = \{\exists\; s \in [0,t) \colon  X_s = 0\}$.
The statistic 
\begin{equation}
	\begin{aligned}
		\varrho_n(X) &= \left(4  \sqrt{\frac 2 \pi} \right) \frac{1}{\sqrt n}\frac{\cD{2}{n,\cdot}(X)}{ \cD{1}{n,\cdot}(X)}
	\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
is a consistent estimators of $\rho $, conditionally on the event $\mathcal H_t $, i.e., $\varrho_n(X)  \longrightarrow  \rho $, in $\Prob^{\mathcal H_t}_x $-probability, as $n \longrightarrow  \infty $.

