body:
[Definition def:APZ of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] A line ensemble $\mathbf{X}$ is asymptotically pinned to zero if for any $ \varepsilon, T > 0$ there is some
$k \in \mathbb{N}$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P} \mleft[ \sup_{t \in [-T,T]} X^k(t) \leqslant \varepsilon \mright] \geqslant 1 - \varepsilon.
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:secondmomentofy1 of arXiv:2509.21253, '\bf Capacity in high dimensional percolation'] For any positive constant $c$, there exists $C>0$, such that for all $L\ge 10K$, $M\ge cL^2$, and $r\ge 2L$, we have 
		\begin{align*}
			\E{Z_{r,L}^2\cdot \1(X_r^{K-\textrm{line-good}}=M)}\leq C\cdot  M^2\cdot L^4\cdot \pr{X_r^{K-\textrm{line-good}}=M}.
		\end{align*}

