[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2606.08325, 'Digit Mixing under Polynomial Maps'] Let \(P\in\mathbb R[x]\) have degree \(d\ge2\).
			There is a constant $\Gamma_0=\Gamma_0(d)$ only depending on the degree of $P$ such that the following holds. Suppose that for all sufficiently large $n$,
			\begin{equation}
				v_n\ge (\log n)^{\Gamma_0} n^{-(d-1)/d}.
			\end{equation}
			Then $P(X)$ is  almost surely absolutely normal. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2606.11271, '\LARGE The $K$-th nearest neighbor random walk on a Poisson point process gets trapped'] On $\cE_n$, there exist $m \in \{1,\dots,n-1\}$, $T \in \cT_m$ and an embedding $x$ of $T$ such that the following holds.
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item For all vertices $v$ of $T$, $|B(x(v),r_M(x(v)) \cap \chi| = M+1$.
		\item For all edges $v \to w$ of $T$, $\|x(w)-x(v)\| \le r_M(x(v))$.
		\item $An \le M \sum_{v} r_M(x(v))$.
	\end{enumerate}

[Proposition prop:eik-box-fragment of arXiv:2608.29708, 'Intuitionistic and Constructive Modal Logics for Classical Modal Logicians'] $\textbf{IK} \cap \mathscr{L}_\Box \nparallel \textbf{KI} \cap \mathscr{L}_\Box$.
  \begin{proof}
    The formula in Proposition (prop:ik-nnbox-to-boxnn of the paper) is not provable in $\textbf{KI}$:
    the countermodel in Proposition (prop:fik-lacks-negdia-to-boxneg of the paper)
    satisfies both the $\Box$-p and $\Diamond$-p conditions and falsifies
    $\neg \neg \Box \neg p \to \Box \neg \neg \neg p$.
    One can also show that $\Box (\varphi \lor \psi) \to (\neg \Box \neg \varphi \lor \Box \psi)$ is provable in $\textbf{KI}$,
    which easily follows from $\textsf{CD}$ and $\Box \neg \varphi \to \neg \Diamond \varphi$,
    but not in $\textbf{IK}$, the countermodel for which is visualized in Figure (fig:boxed-cd-countermodel of the paper).
    \begin{figure}[htb]
      \centering
      \begin{tikzpicture}
        \fill (0, 0) circle (2pt);
        \draw (0, 0) node[left]{$x$};

        \fill (0, 2) circle (2pt);
        \draw (0, 2) node[left]{$x_1'$};
        \draw [thick, ->, rel] (0, 0) to (0, 2);
        \draw (0, 1) node[left]{$\leq$};

        \fill (2, 2) circle (2pt);
        \draw (2, 2) node[left]{$x_2'$};
        \draw [thick, ->, rel] (0, 0) to (2, 2);
        \draw (1, 1) node[right]{$\leq$};

        \fill (4, 2) circle (2pt);
        \draw (4, 2) node[right]{$y_2' \Vdash^{\text{h}} p,\,\not \Vdash^{\text{h}} q$};
        \draw [thick, ->, rel, squig] (2, 2) to (4, 2);
        \draw (3, 2) node[above]{$\sqsubset$};
      \end{tikzpicture}
      \caption{\centering The countermodel for Proposition (prop:eik-box-fragment of the paper).}

    \end{figure}
  \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

