[Defn def:type2constant_TCS of arXiv:2411.10633, 'A Geometric Perspective on the Injective Norm of Sums of Random Tensors'] Given $r\geq 2$ an integer and $2 \leq p < \infty$, we define the type-2 constant  of the $\ell_p$ injective norm of order $r$ tensors  to be the smallest number $\mathcal{C}_{r,p}(d)$  such that for all positive integers $n$ and tensors $T_1, \ldots, T_n \in (\mathbb R^d)^{\otimes r}$, we have\footnote{The sum of squared norms on the right-hand side of (equation eq:type2def_TCS of the paper) have also appeared in [Tom74,AW02] in the context of random matrices as a variance parameter, which is not as precise as the one given in~(equation eq:NCK_TCS of the paper) that gained attention after it appeared in matrix concentration inequalities~[Oli10,Tro10].}
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb E \Big\|\sum_{k=1}^n \varepsilon_k T_k\Big\|_{\mathcal{I}_p}^2 \leq \mathcal{C}_{r,p}(d)^2 \cdot \sum_{k=1}^n \left\lVertT_k\right\rVert_{\mathcal{I}_p}^2 ,
\end{equation}
where $\varepsilon_1, \ldots, \varepsilon_n$ are i.i.d. Rademacher variables, i.e., $ \varepsilon_k = \pm 1$ with probability $\frac12$ each.

[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2609.03830, 'Parabolic Poincar\'e inequalities and maximal function estimates for systems of partial di'] Let $1< p<\infty$, $\max\{1,p-1\}\le q<\infty$ and $\la>0$. Assume that $|F|\in L^{p-1}_{\loc}(\Omega_T)$ and that $u\in  L^q_{\loc}(0,T;W^{1,q}_{\loc} (\Om;\mathbb{R}^N))$ satisfies \eqref{p_weak_sol}
 for every $\varphi\in C_0^\infty(\Om_T;\mathbb{R}^N)$.
Then there exists a constant $c=c(n,q,L)$ such that
	\begin{equation}
    \fiint_{Q}\frac{|u-u_{Q }|^{q}}{\rho^{q}}\,dz \le c\fiint_{Q}|\na u|^{q}\,dz+ c\biggl( \lambda^{2-p}\fiint_{Q} ( |\na u|+ |F| )^{p-1}\,dz \biggr)^q
    \end{equation}
    for every parabolic cylinder $Q=\Qla \Subset\Omega_T$.

