[Corollary 14 of arXiv:2604.22567, 'Sign-balance of random Laplace eigenfunctions'] Assume that either (a) there exists a number $\delta_{0}>0$ so that $\eta(T)>T^{\delta_{0}}$ or (b) $\Mcc=\Sc^{d}$.
There exist numbers $\delta_{1}>0$ sufficiently small and $C_{1}>0$ sufficiently large, so that one has
\begin{equation*}
|K_{T,\eta}(x,y)| \le \frac{C_{1}}{T^{\delta_{1}}},
\end{equation*}
uniformly for every $x,y\in\Mcc$ satisfying $d(x,y) > \frac{1}{T^{1-\delta_{1}}}$, restricted to $d(x,y)\in \left[0,\frac{\pi}{2}\right]$ in case (b). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem Thm:diffbounds of arXiv:2411.13030, 'Classification of the limit shape for 1+1-dimensional FPP'] Let $G$ be non-deterministic and $v\ge 0$. For each $n$, let $\gamma^n(v)$ be the geodesic from the origin to $(n, {\lceil v n \rceil})$. The following bounds hold almost surely:
\begin{equation}

\partial^+ \Lambda(v) \le \liminf_{n \to \infty} \frac 1 n \left( U(\gamma^n(v))+R(\gamma^n(v))-D(\gamma^n(v))\right)
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}

\partial^- \Lambda(v) \ge \limsup_{n \to \infty} \frac 1 n \left( U(\gamma^n(v))-R(\gamma^n(v))-D(\gamma^n(v))\right).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem Chistyakov, G\"otze of arXiv:2411.16103, 'Non-commutative Stein's Method: Applications to Free Probability and Sums of Non-commutati'] Let the notation of Theorem (eq:freclt of the paper) prevail. Let $\mu$ denote the common distribution of the $a_k$ and $\nu_{n}$  the analytic distribution of (equation eq:normalizedSn of the paper). Then we have that 
\begin{align*}
d_{K}(\nu_n,\mathbf{s})
  &\leq \frac{C}{\sqrt{n}}\left(\int_{\mathbb{R}}|x|^3\mu(dx)+\left(\int_{\mathbb{R}}|x|^4\mu(dx)\right)^{1/2}\right),
 \end{align*}
for some universal constant $C>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop 11 of arXiv:2510.24562, 'Hard wall repulsion for the discrete Gaussian free field in random environment on $\mathbb'] Recall $\cC_N$ as in~\eqref{eq:DefinitionCN}. For every $\delta \in (0,1)$ we have that for $\bbQ$-a.e.\ $\omega \in \Omega_{\lambda,\Lambda}$
    \begin{equation}

        \limsup_{N \to \infty} \frac{1}{N^{d-2}\log N} \log \bbP^\omega \left[
            \begin{minipage}{0.35\textwidth}
                \begin{center}
                $\{ z \in \cC_N: z $ is good at level $ a_\delta \}$\\ does not satisfy~\eqref{eq:CoveringProperty} with $\hat{L} = N/(\log N)^{1/4d}$ and $\rho = 1/2$
            \end{center}
        \end{minipage}
        \right] = - \infty \,,
    \end{equation}

