[Lemma lem:benchmark-mixed-excursion of arXiv:2604.24389, '``True" self-avoiding walks on general trees'] For every $K\ge0$, $u\in W_K$ and $z\in E_K$, we have
\begin{equation}
\widehat f_S^{(K)}(1;u,z)-\widehat f_S^{(K)}(s;u,z)
=
\frac{\sqrt2\,A_{K,u}}{\varsigma_\beta}\,H_K(z)\,\sqrt{1-s}
+
o\!\bigl(H_K(z)\sqrt{1-s}\bigr)
\quad \text{as }s\uparrow1.
\end{equation}
Moreover, there exists a constant $C<\infty$ such that for every $z\in E_K$ and every $n\ge1$,
\begin{equation}
f_S^{(K)}(n;u,z)\le C\,A_{K,u}\,H_K(z)\,n^{-3/2},
\end{equation}
and consequently, for every $0\le s<1$,
\begin{equation}
0\le \widehat f_S^{(K)}(1;u,z)-\widehat f_S^{(K)}(s;u,z)
\le C\,A_{K,u}\,H_K(z)\,\sqrt{1-s}.
\end{equation}

[Lemma 59 (Spatial mixing of the Gibbs measure of the SWM) of arXiv:2603.28734, 'Free energy analyticity of the disordered XY model and Debye screening in the 2D Coulomb g'] Fix the dimension $d\in\Z_{\geq 1}$ and the inverse temperature $\beta\in\R_{\geq 0}$.
    Then there exist constants $C<\infty$ and $c>0$ such that
    \[
        \Big\|\mu_{\Lambda_{2n},\beta}^{+1}|_{\Lambda_n}-\mu_{\Lambda_{2n},\beta}^{-1}|_{\Lambda_n}\Big\|_{\operatorname{TV}}
        \leq Ce^{-cn}
    \]
    for all $n\in\Z_{\geq 1}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

