body:
[Theorem 3 (Vanishing-mesh cutoff) of arXiv:2608.15914, 'Absorption cutoff and stationary singularities for rounded Gaussian random dynamical syste'] Assume $0<A<A_c(N)$. Then, for every fixed $a\in\R$,
  \begin{equation}
    \norm{
      P_{\varrho,A,N}^{t_\varrho(a)}(Q_\varrho x_0,\cdot)-\delta_0
    }_{\TV}
    =
    \Pp(\tau_\varrho^{(N)}>t_\varrho(a))
    \to
    \Phi_{\mathrm G}(-a),
    \qquad
    \varrho\downarrow0.
  \end{equation}
  In particular, $Y^{(N)}$ has total variation cutoff to $\delta_0$
  at time $L_\varrho/\gamma_{A,N}$ with window
  $\sigma_N \gamma_{A,N}^{-3/2}\sqrt{L_\varrho}$ and Gaussian profile
  $a\mapsto\Phi_{\mathrm G}(-a)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

