[Proposition prop:Gz of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Let $z\in \mathbb{C}^n$ be fixed. For every $F:\mathscr{F}_z\to \mathbb{R}$ measurable, we have 
  \begin{equation}
    \int_{\mathscr{F}_z} F(f) \rho_{\mathcal{E}^\mathbb{C}}(f)\, \mathrm{d} f=\frac{1}{\pi}\mathbb{E}[F(\mathcal{G}_z)] 
  \end{equation}
  where $\rho_{\mathcal{E}^\mathbb{C}}(f) :=(1/\pi^n)\exp(-|f|^2)$ is the density of $\mathcal{E}^\mathbb{C}\randin \mathscr{F}$ and where
  \begin{equation}
    \mathcal{G}_z:=\mathcal{E}^\mathbb{C}-\frac{\mathcal{E}^\mathbb{C}(z)}{\mathrm{K}^\mathbb{C}(z)}\mathrm{K}^\mathbb{C}(z,\cdot)\randin \mathscr{F}_z
  \end{equation}
  with
  \begin{equation}
    \mathrm{K}^\mathbb{C}(z,z'):=\sum_{a\in A}\overline{f^\mathbb{C}_a(z)}\, f^\mathbb{C}_a(z'), \quad \forall z'\in\mathbb{C}^n.
  \end{equation}

