[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2506.16260, 'Fractional Compound Poisson Random Fields on Plane'] Let $\{N(t),\ t\ge0\}$ be a Poisson process with transition rate $\lambda>0$ which is independent of a two parameter stable subordinator $\{H_\alpha(t_1,t_2),\ (t_1,t_2)\in\mathbb{R}^2_+\}$, $0<\alpha<1$, defined in Section \ref{tpsub}. Then, the SFPRF has the following time-changed representation: 
	\begin{equation}
		N_\alpha(t_1,t_2)\overset{d}{=} N(H_\alpha(t_1,t_2)),\ (t_1,t_2)\in\mathbb{R}^2_+.
	\end{equation}

