[Lemma enormous_bound_lite of arXiv:2606.29622, 'Affine Structure of the Brownian Signature'] Let $Y$ be a real-valued random variable. If the degree of the polynomial $N$ is even with leading coefficient $p_N$ such that  $\, \mathfrak{Re}(p_N) < 0$, then the map $x \mapsto \mathbb{E}\left[\exp({p(x + Y)})\right]$ is entire; that is, there exists a complex sequence $\bm{u} = (\bm{u}^0, \bm{u}^1, \ldots)$ such that
    \begin{align}
\mathbb{E}\left[\exp({p(x + Y)})\right] = \sum_{k\geq 0} \bm{u}^k \frac{x^k}{k!} = \bracket{\bm{u}}{\mathbbm{x}} \,, \quad x \in \mathbb{R}\,.
   \end{align}

[Lemma FAevent_and_unique_crossings of arXiv:2603.28520, 'The Supercritical Loop O(1) and Random Current Models: Uniqueness and Mixing'] Let $\omega \in \{0,1\}^{E(\Lambda_n)}$ and $A\subseteq \partial_v \Lambda_n$, then
\begin{center}
$\omega \in \mathcal{F}_A \cap \mathtt{UC}_n$ if and only if $\omega\vert_{\Lambda_n \setminus \Lambda_{n/2}} \in \mathcal{F}_A \cap \mathtt{UC}_n$. 
\end{center}

[Thm IDLLN of arXiv:2508.07099, 'The Maki-Thompson model with random awareness'] Suppose that $X^n(0)\to X(0)\in E$ almost surely as $n\to\infty$ and define
    \begin{equation}
        X(t)=X(0)+\int_0^tF(X(s))ds.
    \end{equation}
    Then for every $t\geq0$, $\lim_{n\to\infty}\sup_{s\leq t}\Vert X^n(s)-X(s)\Vert_p\to0$ as $n\to\infty$ almost surely.

