body:
[Proposition 35 of arXiv:2608.18075, '2608.18075'] Let $S$ be an almost surely finite stopping time, freeze
$(u_S,\rho_S)$ with $\rho_S\ne0$, and let $M$ be an
$\mathcal F_S$ measurable integer.  There are deterministic
$K_{\rm tr},r_{\rm tr}<\infty$ and $a_{\rm tr},\alpha_{\rm tr}>0$ such
that, on
\begin{align*}
 M\ge M^{(2)}(\rho_S)
       \vee K_{\rm tr}(1+\|u_S\|_{C^\gamma})^{r_{\rm tr}},
\end{align*}
one has
\begin{align}
 \mathbf P\left(
  \|\Pi_0\rho_{S+t_M}\|_2
  \ge a_{\rm tr}M^{-3}
      \|\rho_S\|_{H^{-(\alpha_{\rm H}/2+1)}}
  \;\middle|\;\mathcal F_S\right)
 \ge\alpha_{\rm tr}.

\end{align}
The constants do not depend on $S,M,u_S$, or $\rho_S$.

