[Lemma mainlemma of arXiv:2607.06952, 'Universality for cokernels of partially random integral matrices'] Let $M$ be as in Theorem (thmmoments of the paper), let $\lambda = 2$, and define $D_1,D_2,\theta$ using Definition (defkey of the paper). Let $\zeta > 0$. Then, there exists $K>0$ such that  \begin{equation}
        \#\Sur_{\{n_k\},r}(V,G) \leq K \left(\frac{|G|}{D_1}\right)^{(1-\alpha)n} \left(\frac{|G|}{D_2}\right)^{\alpha n} e^{\zeta n}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2606.31596, 'The Invariant Measure of Multiscale Markov Chains via Fast Arborescence Factorization'] Assume reversibility $\eqref{eq:ydetail}$ of the rates $r_x$.
Suppose there exist two functions $a:X\to(0,\infty)$, $b:Y\to(0,\infty)$ such that
\begin{equation} 
	a(x)\; \nu_x(y) \;=\; b(y)\; \mu_y(x)\,,\quad (x,y)\in V \,.
\end{equation}
Then the effective dynamics \eqref{eq:weff2} is reversible with respect to its unique invariant measure $\bar\pi$, given by
\begin{equation} 
\bar\pi\left(M_y\right) \,=\, \frac{1}{Z}\,b(y)\,,\quad y\in Y 
\end{equation}
where $Z=\sum_{y'\in Y}b(y')$.

