[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2606.02570, 'Stochastic completeness for landmark space'] Suppose the radial scalar function $k\colon [0,\infty)\to\R$ is smooth on $(0,\infty)$. Fix $\lmz\in \Land$ and let $R>0$. We then have, for all $\lm\in B(\lmz,R)$ and all $i,j\in\{1,\dots,n\}$ with $i\not=j$,
    \begin{displaymath}
        \int_{\|x_i-x_j\|}^{\|z_i-z_j\|}
        \frac{\db r}{\sqrt{2\left(k(0)-k(r)\right)}} < R.
    \end{displaymath}

