[Proposition prop:J-opt of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Let $\mu,\nu\in \Lambda_2(\mathbb R^d)$ and set $\mathcal{A}=\Lambda_{\text{glob}}(0,0,\mu)$, $\mathcal{B}=\Lambda_{\text{glob}}(0,0,\nu)$. 
	Let $\gamma_*$ be a L\'evy 2-optimal coupling of $\mu,\nu$. Then the operator $\mathcal{J}_*:=\Lambda_{\text{glob}}(0,0,\gamma_*)$ is an optimal Markovian coupling of $\mathcal{A},\mathcal{B}$. Moreover, the strong duality holds: 
	\begin{align*}
		\omega_2'(x,y;\mathcal{A},\mathcal{B})=\theta_2(x,y;\mathcal{A},\mathcal{B})= \mathcal{C}_2^\Lambda(\mu,\nu). 
	\end{align*}

