[Lemma lm:v-is-concave of arXiv:2605.16162, 'Deconfinement For $\mathrm{SO}(3)$ Lattice Yang--Mills at Strong Coupling'] The function defined in equation (equation eq:log-Wilson-loop of the paper) satisfies the following properties.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $v(R,T)$ is concave in both variables. That is for all $R,T,r,t \in \N$ with $r \leq R$ and $t \leq T$,
        \begin{equs}
            v(R,T) &\geq \frac{1}{2}(v(R+r,T)+v(R-r,T)),\\
            v(R,T) & \geq \frac{1}{2}(v(R,T+t)+v(R,T-t)).
        \end{equs}
        \item The function $v(R,T)$ is subadditive as a function of $T$ and thus 
        \begin{equs}
            V(R):= \lim_{T \to \infty}\frac{1}{T}v(R,T)
        \end{equs}
        exists. In addition, $V(R)$ is concave.
        \item $v(R,T)$ is non-decreasing in both variables and as a consequence $V(R)$ is also non-decreasing.
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:SRBM_d3 of arXiv:2509.20779, 'Diffusive Scaling limit of stochastic Box-Ball systems and P\MakeLowercase{ush}TASEP'] Let $(\zeta_{\lfloor t\rfloor})_{t\ge 0}$ denote the continuous-time SBBS with $d=3$, capacity $c\ge 3$, and  error probability $\varepsilon\in (0,1)$. As $n\rightarrow\infty$, 
			\begin{align}
			(n^{-1/2}(\zeta_{\lfloor \frac{nt}{1-\varepsilon} \rfloor}-nt \mathbf{1}_{3})\,: \, t\ge 0 ) \Rightarrow \mathcal{W} \quad \text{as $n \to \infty$},
			\end{align}
			where $\mathcal{W}$ is an SRBM associated with data $(S, \mathbf{0}, \varepsilon I_{3}, \hat{R}, \delta_{\mathbf{0}})$ with $S = \{x \in \mathbb{R}^3: x_1 \le x_2 \le x_{3} \}$  the 3-dimensional Weyl chamber, 
            \begin{align}
                \hat{R}_{\varepsilon} = \frac{1}{1-\varepsilon}[R_{1},R_{2}]=
                \begin{bmatrix}
                   1-\varepsilon & 0 \\
                   1 & 1-\varepsilon \\
                   0 & 1 
