[Definition 12 (Super-regular pair) of arXiv:2604.05138, 'Convergence rate of $H$-property for step-graphons'] Let $G$ be an undirected graph, and $A,B$ be two disjoint subsets of $V(G)$.
The pair $(A,B)$ is {\bf $(\epsilon,\delta)$-super-regular} if
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
e(X,Y) &> \delta |X||Y|, 
\\
&\text{for any } X \subseteq A,\; Y \subseteq B
\\
&\text{with } |X| > \epsilon |A|,\; |Y| > \epsilon |B|,
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
and, moreover,
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
e(a,B) &> \delta |B|, && \mbox{for all } a \in A, \\
e(b,A) &> \delta |A|, && \mbox{for all } b \in B.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

[Theorem CTSE-O-C of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] For any $\gamma  \in \left[ {0,\frac{1}{3}} \right)$, assume that $\mathrm{Tr} \left( {Q + {Q^{\frac{1}{2}}}{{\left( { - \Delta } \right)}^{\frac{1 + \gamma }{2} + \rho}}{{\left( {{Q^{\frac{1}{2}}}} \right)}^*}} \right) <  \infty$ with $0 < \rho \ll 1$, where $Q$ denotes the covariance operator of ${\mathfrak{W}}\left( {t} \right)$. Then, there exists a stopping time $\mathfrak{t}$ satisfying $\mathbb{P}\left( {0 < {\mathfrak{t}} \leqslant T} \right) = 1 $ such that Eq.(equation 2DEEUGE1 of the paper) admits martingale solutions 
\begin{equation*}
{u }\left( t ,x \right) \in C\left( {\left[ {0,\mathfrak{t}} \right];{C^\gamma }\left( {{\mathbb{T}^2};{\mathbb{R}^2}} \right)} \right) ,\ \ \mbox{with temporal support} \ {\mathrm{supp}_\mathrm{t}} \ u \subset \left[ {0,\mathfrak{t}} \right]   ,\  \mathbb{P}\mbox{-a.s.} ,
\end{equation*}
that manifest the dissipative behavior
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{E}\left( t \right) <  \mathcal{E}\left( 0 \right) + 2 \int_0^t {{{{\left\langle { {u\left( s \right),\mathrm{d}\mathfrak{ W}\left( s \right)} } \right\rangle }_{{\mathbb{T}^2}}}}}  + t \cdot \mathrm{Tr}\, Q , \ \ \forall \, t \in {\mathrm{supp}_\mathrm{t}} \ u ,\  \mathbb{P}\mbox{-a.s.}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

