[Lemma lemma3.9 of arXiv:2412.06246, 'The smallest singular value for rectangular random matrices with Lévy entries'] Fix some $d,r>0$. Let $(g_{i1},g_{i2},\cdots g_{in})$ be a random vector of i.i.d. coordinates. Consider $H\subset\mathbb{R}$ a Borel subset with $H=H_1\cup H_2$ for two Borel sets $H_1,H_2$, where $\operatorname{dist}(H_1,H_2)\geq d$, and $\min(\mathbb{P}(g_{ij}\in H_1),\mathbb{P}(g_{ij}\in H_2))\geq r$. Given any $t>0$ we define 
    $$
h_{(equation lemma3.9 of the paper)}=\frac{1-\delta^{-1/4}}{C_{(equation theorem3.2 of the paper)}}\sqrt{
\frac{r}{16}
}td,
    $$ and let $y\in\mathbb{R}^n$ be a vector which satisfy $\|y\|_2\geq t$, $\|y\|_\infty\leq \frac{2h_{(equation lemma3.9 of the paper)}}{d}$. Let $(g_{i1}',g_{i2}',\cdots,g_{in}')$ be an i.i.d. copy of $(g_{i1},\cdots,g_{in})$. Then 
    \begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\left\{\left|\sum_{j=1}^n \psi_{ij}(g_{ij}-g_{ij}')y_j\right|\leq h_{(equation lemma3.9 of the paper)}\right\}
  \leq 1-\delta^{-1/4}.\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

