[Lemma lem:Mmatrix of arXiv:2607.03639, '\vspace{-0.6in}An AI-Assisted Solution to the Signed BAR Conjecture: Uniqueness in the Har'] The normalized matrix has the Harrison--Reiman form
\begin{equation}
 \widehat R=I-P^T,
 \qquad P\ge0,
 \qquad \rho(P)<1.
\end{equation}
Every principal submatrix $R_{AA}$ is a nonsingular $M$-matrix and $R_{AA}^{-1}\ge0$. In particular, for every nonempty $A\subset J$, the active directions $\{d_i:i\in A\}$ are linearly independent. For $A\subset J$, define
\begin{equation}
 L_Av=v-R_A R_{AA}^{-1}v_A,
\end{equation}
with $L_\varnothing$ equal to the identity. If $A=I(x)$, then $L_A=\mathsf L_x$ is the (unique) linear map from $\mathbb R^d$ to $H_x$ such that $\mathsf L_xv-v\in\operatorname{span}\{R_i:i\in A\}$. Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 L_A R_i=0,
 \qquad i\in A,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 C_{\mathsf L}:=\max_{A\subset J}\left\|I-R_A R_{AA}^{-1}\pi_A\right\|<\infty,
\end{equation}
where $\pi_Av=v_A$ and the expression for $A=\varnothing$ is the identity.

[Lem 18 of arXiv:2604.00190, '2604.00190'] For $\bfb \in \Xi^\nu$, there exists a measurable function $p_\bfb$ from $E$ to $[0, 1]$ such that for $y\in E$, 
\begin{align}
\varrho^{\nu, \bfb}_{p_\bfb}( \bfb (y), y) =1,\qquad 
\rho^{\nu, \bfb}_{p_\bfb}(  x, y)
\begin{cases}
\geq 1,\qquad &x <\bfb(y),\\
\leq 1 ,\qquad &x>\bfb(y). 
\end{cases}

\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

