[Definition eq:controlledRP of arXiv:2607.19037, 'Semiclassical analysis for Yang--Mills \\ random connections on compact surfaces'] Given a rough path \(\mathbf{W}\in \mathcal{C}^\alpha([0,1],\mathfrak{g})\), we say that a path \(Y\) is controlled by \(\mathbf{W}\) if there exists \(Y' \in \mathcal{C}^\alpha([0,1],\mathrm{End}(\mathfrak{g}))\) such that
\begin{equation}
Y_{s,t}=Y'_s W_{s,t}+R^Y_{s,t},
\end{equation}
where the remainder satisfies \(\|R^Y\|_{2\alpha}<\infty\). This defines the space of \emph{controlled rough paths}
\[
(Y,Y')\in \mathcal{D}^{2\alpha}_{\mathbf{W}}([0,1],\mathfrak{g}).
\]

