body:
[Lemma manyquantifiers of arXiv:2607.06813, 'Mixing of Glauber Dynamics on High Overlap Gibbs Measures'] For all $C_1,C_2\geq 0$ and $\delta \in (0,1)$, there exists $\theta,c_3,m_0\geq 0$ such that the following holds: for all $m \geq m_0$, $J \in \mathbb{R}^{m \times m}$ symmetric, $v \in \mathbb{R}^m$, if $\|J\|\leq C_1$ and $\|v\|\leq C_2\sqrt{m}$, the random variable $X$ with quadratic Gibbs distribution on $\{\pm 1\}^m$ given by
    \begin{equation}
    \nu_{J,\theta \mathbf{1}_m +v}(x) \propto \exp\left(\frac12x^\top J x + \theta \mathbf{1}^\top x + v^\top x  \right),
    \end{equation}
    has, with probability at least $ 1-\exp(-c_3m)$, more than $(1-\frac{\delta}2)m$ positive spins.

