body:
[Lemma l.transport of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] {HSTT_vacuum}}]
	Fix any choice of parameters $\tau, \delta, r > 0$ and $x_0, v_0\in \mathbb R^3$ and define the associated trajectory $(x_t,v_0)$ by~(equation e.kinetic_trajectory of the paper) and path by (equation e.path of the paper). Suppose that $g$ is a nonnegative, classical supersolution to~(equation e.kfp_lower of the paper) and that
	\begin{equation}
		g_{\rm in}(x,v) > \delta \qquad \text{for each }(x,v) \in B_r(x_0)\times B_r(v_0).
	\end{equation}
    Then, there exists a universal constant $\mu > 0$ such that whenever
    \begin{equation}
        \tau + \frac{\tau \left\|\mathcal A\right\|_{\rm path}}{r^2} + \frac{\tau \left\|\mathcal B\right\|_{\rm path}}{r} \leq \mu,
    \end{equation}
    there holds
	\begin{equation}
		g\left(\tau,x,v\right) > \frac{\delta}{C_{\rm tran}} \qquad \text{for each }(x,v) \in B_{\nicefrac{r}{4}}(x_{\tau}) \times B_{\nicefrac{r}{4}}(v_0).
	\end{equation}
    The constant $C_{\rm tran}> 0$ depends on only on upper bounds for $\tau$ and $\left\|\mathcal C_-\right\|_{\rm path}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

