[Lemma xj of arXiv:2509.07372, 'On the edge eigenvalues of sparse random geometric graphs'] Let $\mathbf{x}_j=(x_{j1},\cdots,x_{jd})^\top\stackrel{\operatorname{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}_d(\bm{0},\operatorname{diag}(\sigma_1^2,\cdots,\sigma_d^2))$, $j=1,\cdots,n$, with $\sigma_i>0$ for $i=1,\cdots,d$. Then, with probability $1-\oo(1)$, for all $j=1,\cdots,n$ and $i=1,\cdots,d$,
		\begin{align*}
			|x_{ji}/\sigma_i|\leqslant\sqrt{2\log n}.
		\end{align*}

