[Lemma 48 of arXiv:2606.24887, '2606.24887'] Let $M$ and $M^\prime$ be Hermitian matrices. If $z \in \C\setminus \R$ and $0 < \eta \le \eta^{\prime}$ then 
		\begin{equation*}
			\|G(z, M)\| \le \frac{1}{\abs{\Im z}}, \quad 
			\|G(\ii \eta,  M) - G(\ii \eta^\prime, M)\| \le \frac{\eta^{\prime} - \eta}{\eta^2}, \quad  
			\|G(\ii \eta,  M) - G(\ii \eta, M^\prime)\| \le \frac{\|M - M^{\prime}\|}{\eta^2}.
		\end{equation*}

