body:
[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2607.27150, 'Modelling Anomalous Diffusion: The Role of CTRWs and Non-Local Dynamics'] Let $l_t^\alpha (\cdot)$ be the distribution of the inverse $\alpha$-stable subordinator.  Let $P_t$, $t \geq 0$, be a uniformly bounded strongly continuous semigroup on a Banach space $(\mathfrak{B}, \left\| \cdot \right\|)$, associated with the generator $(G, \mathcal{D}(G))$. Then the family of operators $\mathcal{P}_t$, $t \geq 0$, given by
		\begin{align}
			\mathcal{P}_t u = \int_0^{+\infty} P_s u \, l_t^\alpha(ds),
		\end{align}
		is a uniformly bounded family of linear operators from $\mathfrak{B}$ to $\mathfrak{B}$ and the mapping $t \mapsto \mathcal{P}_tu$ solves, whenever $u \in \mathcal{D}(G)$, the problem
		\begin{align}
			\partial_t^\alpha (q(t)-q(0))\, = \, G q(t), \qquad q(0)  = u.
		\end{align}

