[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2608.28964, '2608.28964'] For the equation \eqref{eq V}, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that the following holds. For any $\beta>0$, $N\in\N^+$, $V_0\in \mathcal X$ and $g$ satisfying \eqref{eq g}, the solution $V$ of \eqref{eq V} with the control $h\in H_{0,1}$ given by
	\begin{equation*}
	h(r)=-\left(\mathcal A_{N,g}^*(\mathcal G_{N,g}+\beta)^{-1}\mathcal J_gV_0\right)(r),\quad r\in(0,1),
	\end{equation*}
    satisfies that
	\begin{align}
	\|V(1)\|_{\mathcal X}&\leq\mathcal C_g\left(\widehat b_N\lambda_N\beta^{1/2}+\lambda_N^{-1/4}\right)\|V_0\|_{\mathcal X},\\
	\|h\|_{L^2(0,1;L^2(\omega))}&\leq\mathcal C_g\left(\widehat b_N\lambda_N+\beta^{-1/2}\lambda_N^{-1/4}\right)\|V_0\|_{\mathcal X},
	\end{align}
    where $\widehat b_N:=\max\{|b_j|^{-1}:1\leq j\leq N\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

