  \begin{align*}
    \frac{d}{ds}x^\top \tilde{\phi}(s;t) x\leq  &2x^\top a(t - s)^\top \tilde{\phi}(s; t)x +x^\top S(t-s) x\\
    \leq &2\|a(t-s)\|_2\|\tilde{\phi}(s;t)\|_2|x|^2+\|S(t-s)\|_2|x|^2,
  \end{align*}
  where $\|\cdot\|_2$ is the matrix 2-norm. Thus it follows that 
  \begin{align*}
    \|\tilde{\phi}(s;t)\|_2\leq \int_0^s \left\{ 2\|a(t-u)\|_2\|\tilde{\phi}(u;t)\|_2+\|S(t-u)\|_2 \right\}du.
  \end{align*}
  Hence Gronwall's lemma yields
  \begin{align*}
