[Proposition 65 (Proposition 8.7 in \cite{BP93}) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Suppose that 
    \begin{equation*}
        \bE_n \big[ N(T, t) \big] \xrightarrow{n \rightarrow \infty} \bE_\infty \big[ N(T, t) \big] < \infty
    \end{equation*}
     for all finite trees $t$ and that $\bP_\infty$ is uniquely determined by the values of $\bE_\infty [N(T, t)]$. Then $\bP_n \xrightarrow{d} \bP_\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

