[Theorem thm: recipe of arXiv:2604.05941, 'Banach spaces of continuous paths with finite $p$-th variation'] Fix any $p>1$. Suppose that $h\in C^1([0,1])$ is non-decreasing with $h(0)=0$, and that $\big[(h')^{1/p}\big]^{(p)}_{\mathbb{T}}\equiv 0$. Then, there exists a function $y\in V^p_{\mathbb{T}}$ such that
    \begin{equation}    
        [y]^{(p)}_{\mathbb{T}}(t)=h(t),\qquad \forall\,t\in[0,1].
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, if in addition $(h')^{1/p}\in C^{\alpha}([0,1])$ for some $\alpha\leq \frac1p$, then $y$ is also in $C^{\alpha}([0,1])\cap V^p_{\mathbb{T}}$.

