[Thm Moment Central Limit Theorem of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] Let $M(t)$ be the stationary GOE processes. Then for $k$ fixed times $t_1,\dots ,t_k$ and exponents $j_1, \dots ,j_k$ the vector 
\begin{equation*}
    \left(n^{-j_1/2}\left(\mathrm{Tr}(M(t_1)^{j_1})-\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(M(t_1)^{j_1})]\right),\dots,n^{-j_2/2}\left(\mathrm{Tr}(M(t_k)^{j_k})-\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(M(t_k)^{j_k})]\right)\right),
\end{equation*}
converges both weakly and in the sense of moments to a Gaussian vector, as $n\to\infty$. Moreover, as a process
\begin{equation*}
    \left(n^{-j_1/2}\left(\mathrm{Tr}(M(t)^{j_1})-\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(M(t)^{j_1})]\right),\dots,n^{-j_k/2}\left(\mathrm{Tr}(M(t)^{j_k})-\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{Tr}(M(t)^{j_k})]\right)\right),
\end{equation*}
converges weakly in $C[0,\infty)$ to a Gaussian process. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

