$$g_t(y)-g_t(x)=R_{\lambda_t}(x,y).$$
Therefore $g_t$ is indeed a stretching morphism from $\lambda_t$ ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:db7d513e4865dcb2a0f04bfc8822f96e56ff3bf9aba9e7bf7ef194361e8e6418","revision_digest":"sha256:eab365ac47e54d6331fafdebee643fb1f897445c099ba6f3e0c8229a0173c2fb","source_id":"arxiv:2609.03968","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

body:
[Lemma lem:incidence-bound of arXiv:2608.18293, 'Critical tensor covariance at the Marchenko--Pastur threshold'] Assume $n>2d$. Let $b=(b_I)_{I\in\Omega_{n,d}}\in\mathbb{C}^{\Omega_{n,d}}$ satisfy
\[
  \sum_{I\in\Omega_{n,d}}b_I=0.
\]
Then for $1\le r\le d$,
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{
  \|M_r^{\mathsf T}b\|_2^2
  \le
  \binom{d-1}{r-1}
  \binom{n-r-1}{d-r}
  \|b\|_2^2.}

\end{equation}

