[Theorem 1 (Positive-temperature structure \cite{Lopatto2026}) of arXiv:2607.18032, 'FRSB in the SK spin glass: convergence to full-interval support at zero temperature'] For every $\beta>1$, there exist $q_\beta\in(0,1)$, $c_\beta\in(0,1)$, and a nonnegative function $\rho_\beta\in C^\infty([0,q_\beta))$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \mu_\beta(\mathrm d s)=\rho_\beta(s)\dd s+c_\beta\delta_{q_\beta}(\mathrm d s).

\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation*}
 \supp\mu_\beta=[0,q_\beta]
 \quad\text{and}\quad
 \overline{\supp_{[0,q_\beta)}(\rho_\beta(s)\dd s)}^{\,[0,q_\beta]}=[0,q_\beta],
\end{equation*}
and the atom at $q_\beta$ is the only atom of $\mu_\beta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

