[Lemma lem:BLPP-kernel-reform of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The multipoint distribution satisfies
\[
\det(I - \chi_{\mathbf{a}} K
\chi_{\mathbf{a}})_{L^2(\{t_1, \dotsc, t_k\}
\times \mathbb{R})}
= \det(I - K_{\mathbf{t}, \mathbf{a}, n})_{L^2(\mathbb{R})},
\]
where
\begin{equation}
K_{\mathbf{t}, \mathbf{a}, n}
= \sum_{1 \leq i \leq j \leq k}
\int_{a_i}^{\infty} \int_{a_j}^{\infty}
