\begin{align}

\msf T_0(t)=\tfrac{\msf{A}(D)}{2\pi}t^{-1}
-\tfrac{\msf{L}(\partial D)}{4\sqrt{2\pi}}t^{-1/2}+O(1)\qquad\text{as }t\to0,
\end{align}
where $\msf L(\partial D)$ is the length of the curve
$\partial D$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma Lem3 of arXiv:2412.01070, 'A note on Lévy-driven McKean-Vlasov SDEs under monotonicity'] Assume that  $({\bf H}_1)$, $({\bf H}_{2})$ with $g\equiv{\bf0}$
 and $({\bf H}_{3})$ are satisfied, and suppose that   $Y_0\in L^\beta(\Omega\to\mathbb R^d,\mathscr F_0,\mathbb{P})$.  Then, for any $T,{\varepsilon}>0,$
\begin{align}
\lim_{n,m\to\8}\mathbb{P}\Big(\sup_{t\in[0,T]}|Y_t^{(n)}-Y_t^{(m)}|\ge{\varepsilon}\Big)=0.
