{"artifact_digest":"sha256:cc4fe30506860dda3ae47a72c8b20a85a39fcf92498de03c3786065d3d3619f3","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/cc/cc4fe30506860dda3ae47a72c8b20a85a39fcf92498de03c3786065d3d3619f3.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:192bf2f82c6e751a4eb42e20b233cc31c31e70505b9f7aae1454254cb03f522b","bundle_entry_key":"2607-29423-lemma-26-lmmobsalgequality","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_048","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_048.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2607-29423-lmm-26-lmmobsalgequality","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Without loss of generality we can assume that $\{\tau_j\}_j$ is an increasing sequence.
Notice that if $u, v, w$ lie on $\mathbb{R}$ in increasing order, then
\begin{multline}
\frac{\obs{f}{u}{v}_{0}\obs{f}{u}{w}_{0}}{\obs{f}{v}{w}_{0}} 
= \frac{f'(u) \, |f(w)-f(v)|}{|f(v)-f(u)| \cdot |f(w)-f(u)|} \\
= f'(u)\Biggl(\frac{1}{|f(v)-f(u)|}-  \frac{1}{|f(w)-f(u)|} 
\Biggl).
\end{multline}
