[Lmm lmmGlobalUniqFuncEqual of arXiv:2607.29423, 'Schwarzian Field Theory at High Temperatures'] Let $\Big\{\obs{f}{s_{j}}{t_j}\Big\}_{j=1}^{N}$ be a set of observables (not necessarily non-interlaced) on $[0, T]$ for some $T\in (0, 1)$.
Then we have that for any continuous bounded function $F\in C(\mathbb{R}^N_+)$,
\begin{multline}
\int_{\mathbb{R}} 
\left[
\int_{C[0, T]}
 F\left(\Big\{\obs{\mathsf{Q}_{\xi}}{s_j}{t_j}_0
 \Big\}_{j=1}^{N}
 \right)
\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} \WS{\sigma^2}{a}{T}(\xi) 
\right]
h_T(a, \sigma) \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} a\\
=
\int_{\mathrm{Diff}^1(\mathbb{T})/\mathrm{PSL}(2, \mathbb{R})}
 F\left(\Big\{\obs{\phi}{s_{j}}{t_j}\Big\}_{j=1}^{N}\right) \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathscr{M}_{\sigma^2}(\phi).
\end{multline}

