[Lemma stable_generator_estimate of arXiv:2411.08220, 'Nonlocal operators with Neumann conditions'] Let $\alpha\in (0,2)$. If $f\in C^2(D)$ satisfies
    \[
    \int_D \frac{|f(y)|}{(1+y)^{\alpha+1}}\,\mathrm{d}y <\infty,
    \]    
    then for $x>0$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \lim_{t\to 0^+} \frac{f(x) - P^D_tf(x)}{t}
        = \mathrm{p.v.} \int_D (f(x) - f(y))\nu(x,y)\,\mathrm{d}y + f(x)\nu(x,D^c).
    \end{align*}

