body:
[Defn of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] The GFF is the centered Gaussian process $(\langle \Gamma,f\rangle)_{f\in C_0^{\infty}(D)}$ whose covariance structure is as follows
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb E\left[\langle \Gamma,f \rangle\langle\Gamma,g\rangle\right] = \int_D\int_D G^D (x,y)f(x)f(y)dx dy.
    \end{equation*}

[Lemma PDE_regularity_finite_time of arXiv:2505.21770, 'Gradient-flow SDEs have unique transient population dynamics'] Suppose that the potential of the gradient-flow SDE (equation eq:overdamped_langevin_SDE of the paper) is smooth, i.e. $\Psi \in C^\infty(\mathbb R^d)$. Then, for any positive time $t>0$, it follows that the marginal $p(\cdot, t)$ admits a twice differentiable density, which obeys the Gaussian decay estimates
\begin{align*}
    p(x,t) &\le Kt^{\frac{-d+2}{2}} \exp\bigl(-\frac{\delta}{2t}\|x\|^2 \bigr)\\
    \|\nabla p(x, t)\|  &\le Kt^{\frac{-d+2}{2}} \exp\bigl(-\frac{\delta}{2t}\|x\|^2 \bigr)
\end{align*}
for some $K, \delta > 0$.

