[Corollary 16 of arXiv:2608.19832, 'Sharp Convex Concentration for Symmetric Random Tensors with Subgaussian Coordinates'] Under the assumptions of \Cref{thm:main}, let $M$ be a median of $Z$. If
\[
 1\le u\le c_K\frac n{d^2},
\]
then
\begin{equation}
 \Pp\left\{
 \abs{Z-M}>C_KL n^{(d-1)/2}
 \left(d\sqrt u+\sqrt{d u\log\left(e+\frac nu\right)}\right)
 \right\}
 \le Ce^{-c_Ku}.
\end{equation}

[Defin coherency-eq of arXiv:2510.23430, 'On the Martin boundary for discrete TASEP'] A \emph{coherent system} on $\mathbb{G}^p$ is an element of the projective limit $\varprojlim \mathcal M(\mathbb{G}^p_n)$, that is, a family of measures $\{M_n\in\mathcal M(\mathbb{G}^p_n)\}_{n\geq 0}$ such that for every $\mu\in\mathbb{G}^p_n$ the following coherency relation holds
\begin{equation}

M_n(\mu)=\sum_{\lambda\in\mathbb{G}^p_{n+1}}p^{\downarrow}_{n+1,n}(\lambda,\mu) M_{n+1}(\lambda).
\end{equation}
Using the embedding $\varprojlim \mathcal M(\mathbb{G}^p_n)\to\prod_{n\geq 0}\mathcal M(\mathbb{G}^p_n)$ we define the Borel structure on the set of coherent systems $\varprojlim \mathcal M(\mathbb{G}^p_n)$.

[Lem superstable_log of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $\varphi(x)=-\log\left\lvertx\right\rvert$  and  $\mathsf{P}\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$ with $\int \xi(\Lambda_1)^2\mathsf{P}(d\xi)<\infty$. Then for $n\in \IN$
    \begin{align}
       \int H_n(\xi)\mathsf{P}(d\xi)= \int \frac{1}{2}\sum_{0\neq x\in \xi}g_n(x)\mathsf{P}^0(d\xi).
    \end{align}

