[Thm tt=h+NS of arXiv:2608.26876, 'Local Bousfield classes via homological support'] Let $\cat T$ be a rigidly-compactly generated tt-category and let $A \in \cat T$. Assume that $\pi(\Supph(A))=\Supp(A)$ and that every point of $\Supp(A)$ is weakly visible in $\Spc(\cat T^c)$. The following are equivalent:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item $\LA\cat T$ is relatively tt-stratified;
		\item $\LA\cat T$ is relatively h-stratified and the relative steel condition holds.
	\end{enumerate}

