body:
[Corollary EHI:c:j(r)Counterex of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] Let $X=(X_t)_{t \geq 0}$ be an isotropic unimodal L\'{e}vy jump process on $\mathbb{R}^d$, and let $j(r)$ be its jump kernel. For all $r>0$, let $T^{(r)} := \inf \{ t>0 : |\Delta X(t)| \geq r\}$.
    Suppose there exist sequences $(r_n)$ and $(\rho_n)$ of positive numbers such that
    \begin{itemize}
        \item There exists a $c>0$ (that does not depend on $n$) such that for all $n$,
        \begin{equation}
            \rho_n \geq c r_n.
        \end{equation}
        \item We have \begin{equation}
            1 \gg \mathbb{P}_0 \left( \tau_{B(0, \rho_n)} < T^{(r_n)} \right) \gg \mathbb{P}_0 (|\Delta X(T^{(r_n)})| \leq 4\rho_n+3r_n) .
        \end{equation}
    \end{itemize}
    Then $X$ does not satisfy $\hyperref[EHI:d:ehi]{\mathrm{EHI}}$. Furthermore, if $r_n \to 0$ along a subsequence then $X$ does not satisfy $\hyperref[EHI:d:ehi]{\mathrm{EHI}}(r \leq 1)$, and if $r_n \to \infty$ along a subsequence then $X$ does not satisfy $\hyperref[EHI:d:ehi]{\mathrm{EHI}}(r \geq 1)$.

